Sagacious Method Wizard Feats	KEY:DMC ~ Sagacious Method Wizard Feats	CATEGORY:Internal	DEFINE:Pool_SagaciousWizardFeat|0	BONUS:VAR|Pool_SagaciousWizardFeat|min((WizardLVL/5),4)	BONUS:VAR|Pool_WizardFeat|-min((WizardLVL/5),4)	DESC:Wizard bonus feats may be chosen from the Sagacious Method list (the normal list plus Eschew Materials, Greater Spell Focus, Greater Spell Penetration, Magical Aptitude, Spell Focus, Spell Penetration).


###Block: Spell templates granted by ceremonial feats
Bloodleach	KEY:Spell Template ~ Bloodleach	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellTemplate.SpecialQuality	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Bloodthirsty (DMC)	DESC:Using methods taught by the spirits of slain necromancers, you draw strength from those you wound with your spells. Your veins throb and pulse visibly when you cast a bloodleech spell. This template can be added to any spell that deals hit point damage. The spell deals an additional 1d6 points of damage to one living target of the caster's choice, and the caster is instantly healed of damage equal to this bonus amount. If the chosen target is immune to the type of damage the spell deals or does not suffer the damage for some reason, the caster does not heal any hit points. Using a bloodleech spell against another sentient creature is considered an evil act. [Dragon #311 (Arcane Alterations – Templates for Spells)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1082	BENEFIT:Cost: Verbal component (a specific, guttural, evil-sounding word or phrase) that cannot be modified and a material component (a ruby worth at least 25 gp).
Elemalefic	KEY:Spell Template ~ Elemalefic	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellTemplate.SpecialQuality	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Elemalefic Spellcaster (DMC)	DESC:You have learned how to capture minor elemental spirits and trap them in your spells. A spell amplified by the elemalefic template seems to form frowning skulls, grasping claws, or screaming faces of the appropriate energy type within its area. This template can be added to any spell that deals energy damage (acid, cold, electricity, fire, or sonic). After the spell's normal duration expires, or after its damage is dealt, elemental spirits plague all creatures damaged by the spell for a number of additional rounds equal to the spell's level. This residual energy deals 1d4 points of damage per round of the same energy type as the spell itself dealt. For instance, a creature damaged by an elemalefic ice storm takes 1d4 points of residual cold damage per round for 4 rounds after the spell's duration expires. The spell is still considered to be in effect for the purpose of dispel magic. A spell with this template gains the appropriate energy descriptor (the acid descriptor for an elemalefic acid spell, the cold descriptor for an elemalefic cold spell, and so forth). [Dragon #311 (Arcane Alterations – Templates for Spells)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1082	BENEFIT:Cost: Material component (worth 50 gp) that is specific to the energy type, as follows: a few drops of black dragon drool (acid), diamond dust (cold), a star made of woven copper wire (electricity), ruby dust (fire), or a golden tuning fork (sonic).
Ghost Touch	KEY:Spell Template ~ Ghost Touch	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellTemplate.SpecialQuality	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Ethereal Tendril (DMC)	DESC:You establish a link with the Ethereal Plane. A barely visible, silvery aura briefly surrounds you while you're casting a ghost touch spell. The ghost touch template can be added to any spell with one or more targets. Spells with this template gain the ghost touch property and are not subject to the 50%% miss chance that normally applies against an incorporeal target. [Dragon #311 (Arcane Alterations – Templates for Spells)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1083	BENEFIT:Cost: Material component (silver orb worth at least 50 gp).
Invigorating	KEY:Spell Template ~ Invigorating	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellTemplate.SpecialQuality	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Invigorating Spellcaster (DMC)	DESC:You unlock ancient methods of manipulating divine healing energy. Your eyes turn white while you are casting an invigorating spell. This template can be added to any spell That heals hit point damage. In addition to healing damage normally, an invigorating spell can remove any or all of the following conditions affecting the target(s): dazed, exhausted, fatigued, sickened, and stunned. You specify which conditions are to be removed when you cast the spell. [Dragon #311 (Arcane Alterations – Templates for Spells)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1083	BENEFIT:Cost: Verbal component (recitation of an ancient healing incantation) that cannot be modified.
Shackled	KEY:Spell Template ~ Shackled	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellTemplate.SpecialQuality	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Spellbinder (DMC)	DESC:You have learned how to harness the residual, wasted energy of a spell and use it to hinder the mobility of your targets. The spell energies unleashed by a shackled spell tend to linger even after the spell's effects have taken hold. This template can be added to any spell with a duration other than instantaneous or permanent. In addition to its normal effects, a shackled spell causes each target to move at one--half its normal speed (rounded to the next 5-foot increment) for the entire duration of the spell. If applied to a spell that itself reduces speed (such as slow), the effects are cumulative. Any reduction in speed also affects jumping distance, as normal. [Dragon #311 (Arcane Alterations – Templates for Spells)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1083	BENEFIT:Cost: Somatic component (a grasping hand gesture) that cannot be modified, a material focus (a set of silver shackles worth at least 100 gp), and material component (a golden key worth at least 25 gp). Spells of 9th level are not affected by this template.
Concussive	KEY:Spell Template ~ Concussive	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellTemplate.SpecialQuality	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Spellstrike (DMC)	DESC:You have learned how to direct your destructive spells so that they strike with maximum force. Concussive spells are louder than normal and seem to strike with greater impact. This template can be added to any spell that deals hit point damage. Any creature damaged by a concussive spell must succeed on a Balance check (DC 10 + caster level) or be knocked prone by the impact of the spell. [Dragon #311 (Arcane Alterations – Templates for Spells)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1083	BENEFIT:Cost: Somatic component (thrusting hand gestures) that cannot be modified and a material component (a pearl worth at least 25 gp).
Champion	KEY:Spell Template ~ Champion	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellTemplate.SpecialQuality	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Superior Summons (DMC)	DESC:You have learned ancient magical techniques for imbuing summoned monsters with greater power. Creatures summoned via champion spells appear slightly larger and more powerful than typical specimens of their kind. This template can be added to any conjuration (summoning) spell that summons one or more creatures. All creatures summoned with a champion spell have maximum hit points. Furthermore, you may cast spells with a range of "touch" on any creatures you have summoned without actually needing to touch them, provided that they are within your line of sight. For example, you could cast a blur spell on a creature you have summoned even if it's standing 30 feet away from you. All other parameters (such as range, number of targets, and the like) of a touch spell used in this manner still apply normally. [Dragon #311 (Arcane Alterations – Templates for Spells)]	SOURCEPAGE:p.1083	BENEFIT:Cost: Material component (a topaz worth at least 250 gp)

###Block: Battle Dancer Class Features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Battle Dancer ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Battle Dancer Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=WeaponProfSimple	SOURCEPAGE:p.130	DESC:A battle dancer is proficient with all simple weapons. She is not proficient with any type of armor or shield.
AC Bonus	KEY:Battle Dancer ~ AC Bonus	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Battle Dancer Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:BattleDancerACBonus|0	DEFINE:BattleDancerACStat|0	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|BattleDancerACBonus|PREVAREQ:ENCUMBERANCE,0,var("COUNT[EQTYPE.ARMOR.EQUIPPED]"),0	BONUS:VAR|BattleDancerACStat|max(CHA,0)	BONUS:VAR|BattleDancerACBonus|BattleDancerACStat+floor(BattleDancerLVL/5)	SOURCEPAGE:p.130	DESC:When unarmored and unencumbered, the battle dancer adds her Charisma bonus (if any) to her AC, plus a +1 dodge bonus at 5th level that increases by 1 for every five battle dancer levels thereafter (+%1 now). These bonuses apply even against touch attacks or when she is flat-footed. She loses them when immobilized or helpless, when she wears any armor, carries a shield, or carries a medium or heavy load.|floor(BattleDancerLVL/5)
Unarmed Strike	KEY:Battle Dancer ~ Unarmed Strike	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Battle Dancer Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Improved Unarmed Strike	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|Monk ~ Unarmed Damage	DEFINE:MonkUnarmedDamageLVL|0	BONUS:VAR|MonkUnarmedDamageLVL|BattleDancerLVL	SOURCEPAGE:p.130	DESC:A battle dancer uses unarmed strikes in a manner similar to a monk and gains Improved Unarmed Strike as a bonus feat. Her unarmed attacks deal lethal damage, but she can choose to deal nonlethal damage without penalties on her attack rolls. Treat her attacks as both natural and manufactured weapons for purposes of spells and effects that can enhance either type of attack. Unlike a monk, she does not gain flurry of blows, but she can make an off-hand attack as normal.
Dance of Reckless Bravery	KEY:Battle Dancer ~ Dance of Reckless Bravery	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Battle Dancer Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.131	DESC:All of the battle dancer's allies within 30 feet of her gain a +4 bonus on saves against fear effects for %1 rounds (5 + Charisma modifier). She can use this ability only when she is within an opponent's threatened area. It requires a move action that does not provoke an attack of opportunity.|5+CHA
Bonus Speed	KEY:Battle Dancer ~ Bonus Speed	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Battle Dancer Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:BattleDancerSpeedBonus|0	BONUS:VAR|BattleDancerSpeedBonus|floor((BattleDancerLVL+2)/6)*10	BONUS:MOVEADD|TYPE.Walk|BattleDancerSpeedBonus	SOURCEPAGE:p.131	DESC:The battle dancer gains a +10-foot bonus to speed at 4th level, and additional +10-foot bonuses at 10th and 16th level (+%1 feet now).|BattleDancerSpeedBonus
Dance of the Vexing Snake	KEY:Battle Dancer ~ Dance of the Vexing Snake	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Battle Dancer Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.131	DESC:The battle dancer can use the Tumble skill to move at her normal speed without penalty, and she can Tumble a distance up to her current speed.
Dancer's Strike	KEY:Battle Dancer ~ Dancer's Strike	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Battle Dancer Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.131	DESC:As a standard action at will, the battle dancer generates an aura of energy around her hands and feet that lasts %1 rounds (5 + Charisma modifier). While it lasts her unarmed strikes count as magic for overcoming damage reduction; at 12th level also as one chosen aspect of her alignment, at 18th level also as one chosen special material or alignment.|5+CHA
Dance of the Floating Step	KEY:Battle Dancer ~ Dance of the Floating Step	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Battle Dancer Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.131	DESC:The battle dancer can cross the surface of a liquid, such as water or magma, without taking damage or sinking. If she ends her movement on such a liquid, she takes damage and sinks as normal. She must begin her movement on a stable, firm surface.
Dance of the Springing Tiger	KEY:Battle Dancer ~ Dance of the Springing Tiger	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Battle Dancer Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.131	DESC:When charging, the battle dancer can attempt a DC 20 Tumble check. If she succeeds, she may make a full attack rather than a standard attack as part of her charge.
Dance of the Crushing Python	KEY:Battle Dancer ~ Dance of the Crushing Python	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Battle Dancer Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.131	DESC:The battle dancer must use the Tumble skill to enter her opponent's space without provoking an attack of opportunity. If she succeeds, she may attack her opponent while in its space. If the attack hits, the opponent takes a -2 penalty to AC and cannot make attacks of opportunity until the start of her next action. After the attack, she enters a square of her choice adjacent to the target.
Dance of the Soaring Eagle	KEY:Battle Dancer ~ Dance of the Soaring Eagle	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Battle Dancer Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	MOVECLONE:Walk,Fly,*1	SOURCEPAGE:p.131	DESC:The battle dancer gains a fly speed equal to her base land speed with average maneuverability. If she charges an opponent below her while flying, she gains a +4 bonus on attack rolls and a +2 bonus on damage in place of the normal benefits of charging. She may use her dance of the springing tiger in conjunction with an aerial charge.
Dance of Death's Embrace	KEY:Battle Dancer ~ Dance of Death's Embrace	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Battle Dancer Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.131	DESC:The battle dancer selects a single target within 30 feet and, as a full-round action, performs an elaborate dance that requires a DC 35 Tumble check. If she succeeds, she deals +2d6 points of damage with every successful attack against that target, and any critical threat against it is automatically confirmed. This lasts until the end of her next turn.

###Block: Battle Dancer Dancer's Strike choices
Dancer's Strike (Chaotic)	KEY:Battle Dancer ~ Dancer's Strike (Chaotic)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DancersStrikeAlignment.SpecialQuality	PREALIGN:CG,CN,CE	SOURCEPAGE:p.131	DESC:The battle dancer's dancer's strike aura makes her strikes count as chaotic (as well as magic).
Dancer's Strike (Good)	KEY:Battle Dancer ~ Dancer's Strike (Good)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DancersStrikeAlignment.SpecialQuality	PREALIGN:LG,NG,CG	SOURCEPAGE:p.131	DESC:The battle dancer's dancer's strike aura makes her strikes count as good (as well as magic).
Dancer's Strike (Evil)	KEY:Battle Dancer ~ Dancer's Strike (Evil)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DancersStrikeAlignment.SpecialQuality	PREALIGN:LE,NE,CE	SOURCEPAGE:p.131	DESC:The battle dancer's dancer's strike aura makes her strikes count as evil (as well as magic).
Dancer's Strike (Lawful)	KEY:Battle Dancer ~ Dancer's Strike (Lawful)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DancersStrikeAlignment.SpecialQuality	PREALIGN:LG,LN,LE	SOURCEPAGE:p.131	DESC:The battle dancer's dancer's strike aura makes her strikes count as lawful (as well as magic).
Dancer's Strike (Adamantine)	KEY:Battle Dancer ~ Dancer's Strike Special (Adamantine)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DancersStrikeSpecial.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.131	DESC:The battle dancer's dancer's strike aura also makes her strikes count as adamantine for overcoming damage reduction.
Dancer's Strike (Cold Iron)	KEY:Battle Dancer ~ Dancer's Strike Special (Cold Iron)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DancersStrikeSpecial.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.131	DESC:The battle dancer's dancer's strike aura also makes her strikes count as cold iron for overcoming damage reduction.
Dancer's Strike (Silver)	KEY:Battle Dancer ~ Dancer's Strike Special (Silver)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DancersStrikeSpecial.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.131	DESC:The battle dancer's dancer's strike aura also makes her strikes count as silver for overcoming damage reduction.
Dancer's Strike (Chaotic)	KEY:Battle Dancer ~ Dancer's Strike Special (Chaotic)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DancersStrikeSpecial.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.131	DESC:The battle dancer's dancer's strike aura also makes her strikes count as chaotic for overcoming damage reduction.
Dancer's Strike (Good)	KEY:Battle Dancer ~ Dancer's Strike Special (Good)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DancersStrikeSpecial.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.131	DESC:The battle dancer's dancer's strike aura also makes her strikes count as good for overcoming damage reduction.
Dancer's Strike (Evil)	KEY:Battle Dancer ~ Dancer's Strike Special (Evil)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DancersStrikeSpecial.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.131	DESC:The battle dancer's dancer's strike aura also makes her strikes count as evil for overcoming damage reduction.
Dancer's Strike (Lawful)	KEY:Battle Dancer ~ Dancer's Strike Special (Lawful)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DancersStrikeSpecial.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.131	DESC:The battle dancer's dancer's strike aura also makes her strikes count as lawful for overcoming damage reduction.

###Block: Mountebank (DMC) Class Features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Mountebank (DMC) ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Mountebank (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=WeaponProfSimple|TYPE=ArmorProfLight	SOURCEPAGE:p.384	DESC:A mountebank is proficient with all simple weapons and light armor, but not with any shields.
Beguiling Stare	KEY:Mountebank (DMC) ~ Beguiling Stare	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Mountebank (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:MountebankDC|0	BONUS:VAR|MountebankDC|10+floor(MountebankLVL/2)+CHA	SOURCEPAGE:p.384	DESC:As a standard action, the mountebank stares into her target's eyes. The target must make a Will save (DC %1) or become beguiled until the end of her next turn: he loses his Dexterity bonus to AC and takes a -2 penalty on Will saves and a -5 penalty on Sense Motive checks. At will, but not more than once per day against a single target. A target who saves doesn't notice the attempt unless he makes a DC 20 Knowledge (the planes) check. Mind-affecting.|MountebankDC
Bonus Language	KEY:Mountebank (DMC) ~ Bonus Language	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Mountebank (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ADD:LANGUAGE|1|Abyssal,Infernal	SOURCEPAGE:p.384	DESC:The mountebank gains either Abyssal or Infernal as a bonus language.
Mark of Damnation	KEY:Mountebank (DMC) ~ Mark of Damnation	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Mountebank (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.384	DESC:The mountebank's soul is pledged to an infernal power. Any attempt to return her to life requires a DC 25 Bluff or Diplomacy check (her choice), with a bonus equal to half her mountebank level (+%1).|floor(MountebankLVL/2)
Trapfinding	KEY:Mountebank (DMC) ~ Trapfinding	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:TrapFinding.Mountebank (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.384	DESC:Mountebanks can use the Search skill to locate traps when the task has a Difficulty Class higher than 20, and the Disable Device skill to disarm magic traps (DC 25 + the spell's level). A mountebank who beats a trap's DC by 10 or more with a Disable Device check can study the trap and bypass it without disarming it.
Deceptive Attack	KEY:Mountebank (DMC) ~ Deceptive Attack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Mountebank (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:MountebankDeceptive|0	BONUS:VAR|MountebankDeceptive|floor((MountebankLVL+2)/4)	SOURCEPAGE:p.384	DESC:The mountebank's melee attacks deal +%1d6 damage against a target that is beguiled by her or that she successfully feints (+1d6 at 2nd level, +1d6 every four levels thereafter). Not multiplied on a critical hit, not with ranged weapons or nonlethal damage; it applies even against creatures immune to critical hits or sneak attacks.|MountebankDeceptive
Infernal Patron	KEY:Mountebank (DMC) ~ Infernal Patron	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Mountebank (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:MountebankPatronUses|0	BONUS:VAR|MountebankPatronUses|max(0,floor(MountebankLVL/2)+CHA)	SOURCEPAGE:p.384	DESC:The mountebank can call upon her infernal patron's aid %1 times per day (1/2 her mountebank level + Charisma modifier), each a standard action, to power her mass beguile and infernal abilities.|MountebankPatronUses
Mass Beguile	KEY:Mountebank (DMC) ~ Mass Beguile	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Mountebank (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.384	DESC:Using her infernal patron ability, the mountebank channels a 30-foot burst within %1 feet. Creatures with Hit Dice equal to or less than her level must make Will saves (DC %2) or be beguiled for %3 rounds (her Charisma bonus, minimum 1). Mind-affecting.|100+10*MountebankLVL|MountebankDC|max(1,CHA)
Infernal Guise	KEY:Mountebank (DMC) ~ Infernal Guise	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Mountebank (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.384	DESC:By expending one use of her infernal patron ability, the mountebank can use alter self as a sorcerer with a caster level equal to her mountebank level (%1).|MountebankLVL
Disguise the Soul's Aspect	KEY:Mountebank (DMC) ~ Disguise the Soul's Aspect	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Mountebank (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.384	DESC:When an opponent uses a spell that detects or determines her alignment, the mountebank may expend one use of her infernal patron ability to make a Charisma check opposed by his Sense Motive. If she succeeds, she picks the alignment he detects, and foils his attempts for 24 hours; if she fails, she cannot try again against him for 24 hours.
Infernal Defense	KEY:Mountebank (DMC) ~ Infernal Defense	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Mountebank (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.385	DESC:By expending one use of her infernal patron ability, the mountebank can use displacement upon herself as a sorcerer with a caster level equal to her mountebank level (%1).|MountebankLVL
Infernal Jaunt	KEY:Mountebank (DMC) ~ Infernal Jaunt	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Mountebank (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.385	DESC:By expending one use of her infernal patron ability, the mountebank can slide through planar space like a dimension door, traveling a total of %1 feet (10 feet + 5 feet per mountebank level) as a move action. If she makes a melee attack immediately afterward, she gains her deceptive attack damage against that foe.|10+5*MountebankLVL
Infernal Influence	KEY:Mountebank (DMC) ~ Infernal Influence	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Mountebank (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.385	DESC:By expending one use of her infernal patron ability, the mountebank can use confusion against a single target as a sorcerer with a caster level equal to her mountebank level (%1).|MountebankLVL
Infernal Escape	KEY:Mountebank (DMC) ~ Infernal Escape	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Mountebank (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.385	DESC:By expending two uses of her infernal patron ability, the mountebank can use teleport as a sorcerer with a caster level equal to her mountebank level (%1), on herself only (and a familiar, if she has one).|MountebankLVL
Infernal Deception	KEY:Mountebank (DMC) ~ Infernal Deception	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Mountebank (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.385	DESC:By expending one use of her infernal patron ability, the mountebank can use mislead as a sorcerer with a caster level equal to her mountebank level (%1).|MountebankLVL
Aspect of the Damned	KEY:Mountebank (DMC) ~ Aspect of the Damned	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Mountebank (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.385	DESC:At 20th level the mountebank's soul comes due to her master. She gains the half-fiend template unless already one, her alignment shifts to evil, and she becomes her master's thrall and an NPC under the DM's control - unless a quest breaks her pact. (The template is not applied automatically.)

###Block: Sha'ir Class Features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Sha'ir ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Sha'ir Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=WeaponProfSimple	SOURCEPAGE:p.537	DESC:Sha'irs are proficient with all simple weapons, but not with any type of armor or shield; armor interferes with their arcane gestures (arcane spell failure).
Spells	KEY:Sha'ir ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Sha'ir Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.537	DESC:The sha'ir's spells are retrieved from the elemental planes by his gen: any sorcerer/wizard spell, plus spells of the Air, Chaos, Earth, Fire, Knowledge, Law, Luck, Sun and Water domains (no granted powers). Charisma: DC 10 + spell level + Charisma modifier. A retrieved spell stays ready for %1 hours. Retrieval: a DC 20 Diplomacy check with +%1 (his sha'ir level), +2 for a spell known (arcane), -2 per spell level, -6 for an unknown divine spell, -1 per metamagic level increase, -2 per earlier failure that day; search time 1d4 rounds + spell level (known arcane), 1d6 minutes + 1 per level (unknown arcane, identified with Spellcraft), 1d6 hours + 1 per level (divine). At 4th level and every even level after, he may exchange one known spell for another of the same level. Metamagic needs no longer casting time.|ShairLVL
Summon Gen Familiar	KEY:Sha'ir ~ Summon Gen Familiar	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Sha'ir Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.537	FOLLOWERS:Familiar|1	DEFINE:FamiliarLVL|0	BONUS:VAR|FamiliarLVL|ShairLVL	DESC:At 1st level the sha'ir summons a gen familiar (12 hours, 100 gp of materials) of the elemental type he chooses (air, earth, fire or water), its alignment matching his own. It advances as a familiar of his sha'ir level (its Intelligence should not increase - the familiar table's Intelligence is not suppressed here) and retains the outsider type. If it dies or is dismissed, he must make a DC 15 Fortitude save or lose 200 XP per sha'ir level (half on a success); it can be replaced the next day. Only one familiar at a time.
Recognize Genie Works	KEY:Sha'ir ~ Recognize Genie Works	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Sha'ir Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.538	DESC:The sha'ir can recognize items and magical effects created by geniekind with a DC 20 Knowledge (the planes) check, with a bonus equal to his sha'ir level (+%1).|ShairLVL
Elemental Protection	KEY:Sha'ir ~ Elemental Protection	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Sha'ir Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.538	DESC:The sha'ir has resistance to acid 2, cold 2, electricity 2 and fire 2, damage reduction 2/- against attacks by creatures with the air, earth, fire or water subtype, and a +2 bonus on saves against acid, cold, electricity and fire attacks. Against his gen's energy and creatures of his gen's subtype, the resistance and damage reduction are 4 and the save bonus +4.
Call Janni	KEY:Sha'ir ~ Call Janni	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Sha'ir Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.538	DESC:Once per day, the sha'ir can call a janni, as lesser planar ally (only a janni), caster level %1. He pays the XP cost and bargains as normal.|ShairLVL
Elemental Travel	KEY:Sha'ir ~ Elemental Travel	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Sha'ir Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.538	DESC:The sha'ir can plane shift %1/day (at will from 18th level) to any elemental plane or from one to the Material Plane, caster level %2.|ShairTravelUses|ShairLVL
Call Genie	KEY:Sha'ir ~ Call Genie	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Sha'ir Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.538	DESC:Once per day, the sha'ir can call one dao, djinni, efreeti or marid, or two jann, as planar ally, caster level %1. He pays the XP cost and bargains as normal.|ShairLVL
Craft Genie Prison	KEY:Sha'ir ~ Craft Genie Prison	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Sha'ir Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.538	DESC:The sha'ir gains the benefit of Craft Wondrous Item for genie prisons only (made like an iron flask, holding only geniekind).

###Block: Sha'ir gen choice
Air Gen	KEY:Sha'ir ~ Air Gen	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ShairGen.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.539	DESC:The sha'ir's gen familiar is an air gen (immune to electricity). From 5th level his elemental protection is 4 against electricity and creatures of the air subtype, with a +4 save bonus against electricity.	COMPANIONLIST:Familiar|Companion ~ Air Gen
Earth Gen	KEY:Sha'ir ~ Earth Gen	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ShairGen.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.539	DESC:The sha'ir's gen familiar is an earth gen (immune to acid). From 5th level his elemental protection is 4 against acid and creatures of the earth subtype, with a +4 save bonus against acid.	COMPANIONLIST:Familiar|Companion ~ Earth Gen
Fire Gen	KEY:Sha'ir ~ Fire Gen	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ShairGen.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.539	DESC:The sha'ir's gen familiar is a fire gen (immune to fire). From 5th level his elemental protection is 4 against fire and creatures of the fire subtype, with a +4 save bonus against fire.	COMPANIONLIST:Familiar|Companion ~ Fire Gen
Water Gen	KEY:Sha'ir ~ Water Gen	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ShairGen.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.539	DESC:The sha'ir's gen familiar is a water gen (immune to cold). From 5th level his elemental protection is 4 against cold and creatures of the water subtype, with a +4 save bonus against cold.	COMPANIONLIST:Familiar|Companion ~ Water Gen

###Block: Savant Class Features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Savant ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Savant Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=WeaponProfMartial|TYPE=ArmorProfLight|TYPE=ShieldProf	SOURCEPAGE:p.525	DESC:A savant is proficient with all simple and martial weapons, light armor and all shields except tower shields.
Academic Lore	KEY:Savant ~ Academic Lore	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Savant Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:SavantAcademicLore|0	BONUS:VAR|SavantAcademicLore|SavantLVL+INT	SOURCEPAGE:p.525	DESC:The savant may make a special academic lore check with a bonus equal to his savant level + his Intelligence modifier (+%1) to see whether he knows some relevant information about a situation, person, item, historical event or other subject. If he fails, he must gain a savant level before trying again on that question. He can use both this and a relevant Knowledge check on the same question.|SavantAcademicLore
Skill Assistance	KEY:Savant ~ Skill Assistance	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Savant Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:SavantAssistRange|0	BONUS:VAR|SavantAssistRange|5*(1+floor(SavantLVL/4))	SOURCEPAGE:p.525	DESC:At 1st level, 4th level and every 4 levels thereafter, the savant chooses one of Balance, Climb, Disguise, Hide, Listen, Move Silently, Ride, Spot, Swim in which he has at least 1 rank. Up to his Intelligence modifier allies within %1 feet may replace their check in a chosen skill with a special check using his ranks + their own modifiers and his secret d20 roll (no taking 10 or 20, not for aid another).|SavantAssistRange
Trapfinding	KEY:Savant ~ Trapfinding	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:TrapFinding.Savant Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.526	DESC:Savants can use the Search skill to locate traps with a DC higher than 20, and the Disable Device skill to disarm magic traps (DC 25 + the spell's level). A savant who beats a trap's DC by 10 or more with Disable Device can bypass it.
Talent Lore	KEY:Savant ~ Talent Lore	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Savant Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.526	DESC:The savant gains a bonus feat at 2nd level and every five levels thereafter (7th, 12th, 17th).
Sneak Attack	KEY:Savant ~ Sneak Attack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Savant Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:SneakAttackDice|0	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Sneak Attack	BONUS:VAR|SneakAttackDice|floor((SavantLVL+3)/6)	SOURCEPAGE:p.526	DESC:+1d6 at 3rd level, +1d6 every six savant levels thereafter (+%1d6 from savant levels); stacks with other sneak attack dice.|floor((SavantLVL+3)/6)
Arcane Lore	KEY:Savant ~ Arcane Lore	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Savant Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.526	DESC:From 5th level the savant prepares arcane spells from the savant arcane spell list (Intelligence 10 + spell level to learn, prepare or cast; DC 10 + spell level + Int modifier; bonus spells from Intelligence), without a spellbook. At 5th level and each level after he learns two arcane spells he can cast. A 0 in the progression means bonus spells only. Caster level: half his savant level (%1).|floor(SavantLVL/2)
Divine Lore	KEY:Savant ~ Divine Lore	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Savant Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.527	DESC:From 10th level the savant also prepares divine spells from the savant divine spell list (Wisdom 10 + spell level; DC 10 + spell level + Wis modifier; bonus spells from Wisdom), learning two divine spells per level, prepared with his arcane ones. Arcane and divine slots are kept separately. In this data both lists form one savant list with the two progressions added, Intelligence-based; the divine-only spells use Wisdom for their save DCs.

###Block: Savant skill assistance choices
Skill Assistance (Balance)	KEY:Savant ~ Skill Assistance (Balance)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SavantSkillAssistance.SpecialQuality	PRESKILL:1,Balance=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.525	DESC:The savant can lend his ranks in Balance to allies (skill assistance).
Skill Assistance (Climb)	KEY:Savant ~ Skill Assistance (Climb)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SavantSkillAssistance.SpecialQuality	PRESKILL:1,Climb=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.525	DESC:The savant can lend his ranks in Climb to allies (skill assistance).
Skill Assistance (Disguise)	KEY:Savant ~ Skill Assistance (Disguise)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SavantSkillAssistance.SpecialQuality	PRESKILL:1,Disguise=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.525	DESC:The savant can lend his ranks in Disguise to allies (skill assistance).
Skill Assistance (Hide)	KEY:Savant ~ Skill Assistance (Hide)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SavantSkillAssistance.SpecialQuality	PRESKILL:1,Hide=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.525	DESC:The savant can lend his ranks in Hide to allies (skill assistance).
Skill Assistance (Listen)	KEY:Savant ~ Skill Assistance (Listen)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SavantSkillAssistance.SpecialQuality	PRESKILL:1,Listen=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.525	DESC:The savant can lend his ranks in Listen to allies (skill assistance).
Skill Assistance (Move Silently)	KEY:Savant ~ Skill Assistance (Move Silently)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SavantSkillAssistance.SpecialQuality	PRESKILL:1,Move Silently=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.525	DESC:The savant can lend his ranks in Move Silently to allies (skill assistance).
Skill Assistance (Ride)	KEY:Savant ~ Skill Assistance (Ride)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SavantSkillAssistance.SpecialQuality	PRESKILL:1,Ride=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.525	DESC:The savant can lend his ranks in Ride to allies (skill assistance).
Skill Assistance (Spot)	KEY:Savant ~ Skill Assistance (Spot)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SavantSkillAssistance.SpecialQuality	PRESKILL:1,Spot=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.525	DESC:The savant can lend his ranks in Spot to allies (skill assistance).
Skill Assistance (Swim)	KEY:Savant ~ Skill Assistance (Swim)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SavantSkillAssistance.SpecialQuality	PRESKILL:1,Swim=1	SOURCEPAGE:p.525	DESC:The savant can lend his ranks in Swim to allies (skill assistance).

###Block: Death Master Class Features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Death Master ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Death Master Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|Club|Crossbow (Heavy)|Crossbow (Light)|Dagger|Scimitar|Scythe|Sickle|Quarterstaff	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=ArmorProfLight	SOURCEPAGE:p.186	DESC:A death master is proficient with the club, crossbow (light and heavy), dagger, scimitar, scythe, sickle and quarterstaff, and with light armor, but not with shields.
Bonus Language	KEY:Death Master ~ Bonus Language	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Death Master Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	AUTO:LANG|Abyssal	SOURCEPAGE:p.186	DESC:The death master gains Abyssal as a bonus language; his spells and tomes are written in it.
Rebuke Undead	KEY:Death Master ~ Rebuke Undead	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Death Master Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Basic Turning	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Rebuke Undead	BONUS:VAR|TurnLevelBase,TurnDamagePlusBase|DeathMasterLVL	BONUS:VAR|TurnTimesBase|3+CHA|TYPE=Base	BONUS:VAR|TurnCheckBase|CHA|TYPE=Base	SOURCEPAGE:p.186	DESC:The death master can rebuke undead %1 times per day (3 + Charisma modifier), as an evil cleric of his death master level. With 5 or more ranks in Knowledge (religion) he gains a +2 bonus on rebuking checks.|3+CHA
Spells	KEY:Death Master ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Death Master Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.186	DESC:The death master prepares arcane spells from the death master spell list like a wizard (Intelligence 10 + spell level; DC 10 + spell level + Int modifier; bonus spells from Intelligence) and keeps spellbooks like a wizard's: all 0-level death master spells plus three 1st-level spells and one per Intelligence bonus point to begin with, two new spells per level. Using a vial of blood from an intelligent creature sacrificed to Orcus as material component, he casts without somatic components and so ignores arcane spell failure in armor (8 vials per Medium creature, viable one day).
Undead Minion	KEY:Death Master ~ Undead Minion	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Death Master Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:DeathMasterMinionHD|0	BONUS:VAR|DeathMasterMinionHD|2*floor((DeathMasterLVL-1)/4)	SOURCEPAGE:p.187	DESC:Orcus grants the death master an undead minion (typically a wolf skeleton or a troglodyte zombie; with the DM's permission another skeleton or zombie of CR 1 or lower, or a stronger servitor with a level modifier). It obeys without fail and spies for Orcus; if destroyed or dismissed, a new one appears 24 hours later. At his level it has +%1 bonus Hit Dice and +%1 Strength and Dexterity (no size increase) and: turn resistance +4 (1st), unholy might (5th), persistent corruption (9th), link of the grave (13th), relentless undead (17th).|DeathMasterMinionHD	FOLLOWERS:Undead Minion|1	DEFINE:UndeadMinionLVL|0	BONUS:VAR|UndeadMinionLVL|DeathMasterLVL	COMPANIONLIST:Undead Minion|Skeleton (Wolf),Zombie (Troglodyte)	COMPANIONLIST:Undead Minion|Zombie (Bugbear),Ghoul,Skeleton (Owlbear)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-3	COMPANIONLIST:Undead Minion|Skeleton (Chimera),Zombie (Minotaur),Zombie (Ogre),Zombie (Wyvern)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-6	COMPANIONLIST:Undead Minion|Allip,Skeleton (Ettin),Ghoul (Ghast),Zombie (Gray Render),Wight|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-9	COMPANIONLIST:Undead Minion|Skeleton (Cloud Giant),Mummy,Wraith|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-12	COMPANIONLIST:Undead Minion|Spectre|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-15
Master of the Dead	KEY:Death Master ~ Master of the Dead	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Death Master Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:DeathMasterDC|0	BONUS:VAR|DeathMasterDC|10+floor(DeathMasterLVL/2)+CHA	SOURCEPAGE:p.187	DESC:An undead creature must make a Will save (DC %1) to attack the death master in any way; if it fails, it cannot take aggressive action against him for 24 hours (it could still order minions or cast spells to aid others). Undead without Intelligence automatically fail unless controlled by another creature, which saves for them.|DeathMasterDC
Sustenance of the Dead	KEY:Death Master ~ Sustenance of the Dead	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Death Master Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.187	DESC:Once per round as a free action, the death master can reduce a controlled undead within 60 feet to dust and gain 2 temporary hit points per Hit Die (for 1 hour). An intelligent undead may make a Will save (DC %1) to avoid this; if it succeeds, it is no longer under his control.|DeathMasterDC
Aspect of the Dead	KEY:Death Master ~ Aspect of the Dead	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Death Master Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	VISION:Darkvision (60')	SOURCEPAGE:p.187	DESC:The death master gains darkvision 60 feet and immunity to mind-affecting effects, poison, sleep effects, paralysis, stunning, disease and death effects.
Lichdom	KEY:Death Master ~ Lichdom	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Death Master Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.187	DESC:At 20th level the death master gains the lich template (even if nonhumanoid); an already undead death master gains the lich's armor class, special attacks, turn resistance, damage reduction, abilities and skills. (The template is not applied automatically.)

###Block: Jester Class Features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Jester ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Jester Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|Rapier|Sap|Sword (Short)|Shortbow|Whip	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=WeaponProfSimple|TYPE=ArmorProfLight|TYPE=ShieldProf	SOURCEPAGE:p.320	DESC:A jester is proficient with all simple weapons, plus the rapier, sap, short sword, shortbow and whip, with light armor and all shields except tower shields.
Spells	KEY:Jester ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Jester Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.320	DESC:The jester casts arcane spells from the jester spell list like a sorcerer or bard, without preparing them (Charisma 10 + spell level; DC 10 + spell level + Cha modifier; bonus spells from Charisma; a 0 in the table means bonus spells only). At 5th level and every three levels after, he may exchange one known spell for another.
Jester's Audacity	KEY:Jester ~ Jester's Audacity	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Jester Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:JesterAudacity|0	BONUS:VAR|JesterAudacity|min(1+floor(JesterLVL/5),max(0,CHA))	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|JesterAudacity|TYPE=Dodge	SOURCEPAGE:p.320	DESC:The jester gains a dodge bonus to his Armor Class: +1 at 1st level, +2 at 5th, +3 at 10th, +4 at 15th, +5 at 20th, but never more than his Charisma bonus (+%1 now).|JesterAudacity
Jester's Performance	KEY:Jester ~ Jester's Performance	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Jester Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:JesterDC|0	BONUS:VAR|JesterDC|10+floor(JesterLVL/2)+CHA	SOURCEPAGE:p.320	DESC:Once per day per jester level (%1/day), the jester can use his wit to produce magical effects (standard action to start; he must keep up puns, insults or jokes). He needs at least 1 rank in Perform (comedy), must share a language with and be able to speak to the targets, and can't cast spells or activate items by spell completion or command word meanwhile. Deaf: 20%% failure. Save DC of his performances: %2.|JesterLVL|JesterDC
Fascinate	KEY:Jester ~ Fascinate	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Jester Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.320	DESC:With 3 ranks in Perform (comedy), the jester can fascinate %1 creatures within 90 feet that can see and hear him (one, plus one per three levels beyond 1st), for up to %2 rounds; Will save DC %3 negates (immune for 24 hours). Fascinated creatures take -4 on reactive skill checks; any obvious threat breaks the effect. Enchantment (compulsion), language-dependent, mind-affecting.|1+floor((JesterLVL-1)/3)|JesterLVL|JesterDC
Inspiring Quip	KEY:Jester ~ Inspiring Quip	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Jester Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.321	DESC:With 3 ranks in Perform (comedy), as an immediate action when an opponent misses an attack the jester can see, all allies within 30 feet gain a +2 morale bonus on attacks against that foe for the rest of the encounter.
Taunt	KEY:Jester ~ Taunt	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Jester Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.321	DESC:With 3 ranks in Perform (comedy), the jester taunts one creature within 60 feet that shares a language and can hear him; Will save DC %1. On a failure it gains +1 morale on attacks and -2 AC and must take the most direct route toward the jester (charging if able) on its next turn; provoking an attack of opportunity on the way gives it a new save at +2. The jester must use a free action each round to continue. Mind-affecting, language-dependent.|JesterDC
Calming Performance	KEY:Jester ~ Calming Performance	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Jester Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.321	DESC:With 9 ranks in Perform (comedy), the jester can make all creatures he has fascinated friendly toward him, his allies and each other for %1 minutes. Mind-affecting, language-dependent.|10*JesterLVL
Buffoonery	KEY:Jester ~ Buffoonery	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Jester Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.321	DESC:With 12 ranks in Perform (comedy), the jester distracts one target within 30 feet that can see and hear him: Will save DC %1 each round he keeps it up (free action) or the target loses its Dexterity bonus to AC; a successful save ends it and makes the target immune for 24 hours.|JesterDC
Bone Rattler	KEY:Jester ~ Bone Rattler	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Jester Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.321	DESC:The jester's mind-affecting performance abilities work against undead with Intelligence scores, which gain a +2 bonus on their saves; undead without Intelligence and creatures immune to mind-affecting effects remain immune.
Vicious Lampoon	KEY:Jester ~ Vicious Lampoon	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Jester Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.321	DESC:With 15 ranks in Perform (comedy), every opponent within 60 feet that can hear and understand the jester must make a Will save (DC %1) or take -2 on attack rolls, skill and ability checks and saving throws while he performs (move action), up to %2 rounds. Mind-affecting, language-dependent.|JesterDC|JesterLVL
Vexing Dialogue	KEY:Jester ~ Vexing Dialogue	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Jester Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.321	DESC:With 18 ranks in Perform (comedy), the jester forces one target to make a Concentration check opposed by his Perform (comedy) check to cast a spell, use a supernatural ability or do anything else that would require a Concentration check if it took damage; lasts 1 round, once per encounter per target. Mind-affecting, language-dependent.
Scathing Wit	KEY:Jester ~ Scathing Wit	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Jester Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.321	DESC:With 21 ranks in Perform (comedy), the jester demoralizes one target that can see and hear him: Will save DC %1 or a penalty equal to his Charisma bonus (%2) on attack rolls and saving throws while he performs (move action), up to %3 rounds. Mind-affecting, language-dependent.|JesterDC|max(0,CHA)|floor(JesterLVL/2)

###Block: Nightstalker Class Features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Nightstalker ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Nightstalker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|Crossbow (Hand)|Rapier|Shortbow|Sword (Short)	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=WeaponProfSimple|TYPE=ArmorProfLight|TYPE=ShieldProf	SOURCEPAGE:p.391	DESC:The nightstalker is proficient with all simple weapons plus the hand crossbow, rapier, shortbow and short sword, with light armor and shields except tower shields.
Spells	KEY:Nightstalker ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Nightstalker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.391	DESC:The nightstalker casts divine spells as a mystic does, without preparing them, drawn from the nightstalker spell list (Charisma 10 + spell level to cast; DC 10 + spell level + Charisma modifier), with bonus spells per day from Wisdom (a 0 in the table means bonus spells only). He knows every spell on the nightstalker list of the levels he can cast.
Death Sight	KEY:Nightstalker ~ Death Sight	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Nightstalker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=ATWILL|CASTERLEVEL=NightstalkerLVL|Detect Undead	SOURCEPAGE:p.391	DESC:At will, the nightstalker may use detect undead as the spell.
Trapfinding	KEY:Nightstalker ~ Trapfinding	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:TrapFinding.Extraordinary.Nightstalker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.391	DESC:Identical to the rogue ability: the nightstalker can use Search to locate traps with a DC higher than 20, and Disable Device to disarm magic traps (DC 25 + the spell's level); beating a trap's DC by 10 or more lets him bypass it.
Spiritual Resilience	KEY:Nightstalker ~ Spiritual Resilience	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Nightstalker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:NightstalkerResilience|0	BONUS:VAR|NightstalkerResilience|1+(NightstalkerLVL>=8)+(NightstalkerLVL>=14)	SOURCEPAGE:p.391	DESC:+%1 morale bonus on saving throws against negative energy and necromantic spells and effects (+1 at 1st level, +2 at 8th, +3 at 14th).|NightstalkerResilience
Whispers of the Dead	KEY:Nightstalker ~ Whispers of the Dead	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Nightstalker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:NightstalkerWhispers|0	BONUS:VAR|NightstalkerWhispers|2*floor((NightstalkerLVL+3)/6)	SOURCEPAGE:p.391	DESC:In an enclosed area where five or more creatures have died, the spirits whisper to the nightstalker: a +%1 insight bonus on initiative checks and all Knowledge, Listen, Search and Spot checks (+2 at 3rd level, +4 at 9th, +6 at 15th).|NightstalkerWhispers
Rebuke Undead	KEY:Nightstalker ~ Rebuke Undead	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Nightstalker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Basic Turning	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Rebuke Undead	BONUS:VAR|TurnLevelBase,TurnDamagePlusBase|NightstalkerLVL-3	BONUS:VAR|TurnTimesBase|3+CHA|TYPE=Base	BONUS:VAR|TurnCheckBase|CHA|TYPE=Base	SOURCEPAGE:p.391	DESC:From 4th level the nightstalker may rebuke or command undead as a cleric of his level - 3 (%1), even if good-aligned, %2 times per day.|NightstalkerLVL-3|3+CHA
Advanced Learning	KEY:Nightstalker ~ Advanced Learning	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Nightstalker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.391	DESC:At 5th, 11th and 17th level the nightstalker adds a necromancy or divination spell from the cleric/mystic or sorcerer/wizard list to his nightstalker list (no higher than the highest level he can cast; the lower level if on both lists; no alignment descriptor opposed to his own). (Record the chosen spells with the DM; they are not added automatically.)
Spirit Companion	KEY:Nightstalker ~ Spirit Companion	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Nightstalker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:NightstalkerCompanions|0	BONUS:VAR|NightstalkerCompanions|1+(NightstalkerLVL>=12)+(NightstalkerLVL>=18)	SOURCEPAGE:p.391	DESC:The nightstalker gains %1 ghost cohort(s) (Monster Manual ghost template) of his alignment, from any PC race (level adjustment counts as Hit Dice), each with at most %2 Hit Dice (character level - 3, minus 1 per additional companion). A permanently destroyed companion is replaced only after another nightstalker level; companions advance like cohorts.|NightstalkerCompanions|TL-2-NightstalkerCompanions
Spectral Symbiosis	KEY:Nightstalker ~ Spectral Symbiosis	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Nightstalker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.392	DESC:The nightstalker becomes immune to negative energy damage, level drain, the corrupting touch of undead and necromantic spells and effects; his weapons (including natural weapons and unarmed strikes) and armor have the ghost touch quality while in his possession.

###Block: Urban Druid Class Features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Urban Druid ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Urban Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|Club|Crossbow (Hand)|Crossbow (Light)|Crossbow (Heavy)|Crossbow (Repeating Light)|Crossbow (Repeating Heavy)|Dagger|Quarterstaff|Rapier|Sap|Sword (Short)	AUTO:ARMORPROF|Padded|Leather|Studded Leather	AUTO:SHIELDPROF|SHIELDTYPE=Buckler	SOURCEPAGE:p.631	DESC:Urban druids are proficient with the club, crossbows, dagger, quarterstaff, rapier, sap and short sword, with padded, leather and studded leather armor (the DM may allow other light armor of less than +4) and bucklers. In prohibited armor or with a prohibited shield she can't cast urban druid spells or use her supernatural abilities while doing so and for 24 hours after.
Spells	KEY:Urban Druid ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Urban Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.631	DESC:The urban druid prepares and casts divine spells from the urban druid spell list like a cleric (from the whole list, without domains), Charisma-based (Charisma 10 + spell level; DC 10 + spell level + Cha modifier; bonus spells from Charisma). She can't cast spells of an alignment opposed to her own or her deity's. Her divine focus is a manufactured item common to a city.
Spontaneous Casting	KEY:Urban Druid ~ Spontaneous Casting	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Urban Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.631	DESC:The urban druid can lose a prepared spell to cast any repair spell (repair minor/light/moderate/serious/critical damage and their mass versions) of the same level or lower.
City Sense	KEY:Urban Druid ~ City Sense	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Urban Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SKILL|Gather Information,Knowledge (Local)|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.631	DESC:An urban druid gains a +2 bonus on Gather Information and Knowledge (local) checks.
Favored City	KEY:Urban Druid ~ Favored City	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Urban Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:UrbanDruidFavoredCities|0	BONUS:VAR|UrbanDruidFavoredCities|1+floor(UrbanDruidLVL/4)	SOURCEPAGE:p.631	DESC:The urban druid has %1 favored cities (one at 1st level, another at 4th, 8th, 12th, 16th and 20th; settlements of small-town size or larger she has visited). Within one, she gains a sacred bonus equal to her Wisdom modifier (+%2) on Bluff, Diplomacy, Gather Information and Intimidate checks and a +2 morale bonus on Will saves.|UrbanDruidFavoredCities|max(0,WIS)
Urban Companion	KEY:Urban Druid ~ Urban Companion	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Urban Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Animal Companion	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|DMC ~ Animal Companion Alternate	BONUS:VAR|AnimalCompanionLVL|UrbanDruidLVL	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Bat,Dire Animal (Dire Rat),Rat,Cat,Dog,Dog (Riding),Horse (Light),Horse (Heavy),Monstrous Centipede (Medium),Monstrous Scorpion (Small),Monstrous Spider (Small),Mule,Owl,Pony,Raven,Snake (Viper/Small),Snake (Viper/Medium),Horse (Warhorse Light),Animated Object (Small)	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Animated Object (Medium)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-3	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Animated Object (Large)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-6	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Animated Object (Huge)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-9	SOURCEPAGE:p.631	DESC:The urban druid has an urban companion that advances as a druid's animal companion: bat, dire rat, rat, cat, dog, riding dog, light or heavy horse, Medium monstrous centipede, Small monstrous scorpion or spider, mule, owl, pony, raven, Small or Medium viper, light warhorse, or a Small animated object (a vermin companion has Intelligence 1 and the animal type; a construct companion is created by the 24-hour prayer). From 4th level she may choose from alternative lists with a lower effective level (e.g. Medium animated object at level - 3, Large at - 6, Huge at - 9).
Crowdwalk	KEY:Urban Druid ~ Crowdwalk	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Urban Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.632	DESC:The urban druid moves through crowds as if through open space; moving through a square occupied by a hostile creature (Tumble, overrun) she gains a +4 bonus on the skill check, Strength check or attack roll.
Alley Fighting	KEY:Urban Druid ~ Alley Fighting	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Urban Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.632	DESC:Fighting in an area no wider than her space, the urban druid gains a +1 competence bonus on attack rolls; her melee target around a corner gets no cover (unless total cover), while she keeps hers.
Disease Immunity	KEY:Urban Druid ~ Disease Immunity	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Urban Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.632	DESC:The urban druid is immune to all diseases, including supernatural diseases like mummy rot.
Urban Shape	KEY:Urban Druid ~ Urban Shape	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Urban Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.632	DESC:As a druid's wild shape, %1/day, into Small or Medium humanoids or non-construct creatures of her urban companion list (Large from 8th level, Tiny from 11th, Huge from 15th; Hit Dice no more than her urban druid level). From 12th level also into an object (hardness up to 10; no locomotion or speech). From 16th level, %2/day additionally into a Small to Huge animated object (Gargantuan at 20th), gaining its extraordinary attacks and qualities and the construct type.|UrbanShapeUses|UrbanShapeObject
Information Network	KEY:Urban Druid ~ Information Network	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Urban Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.632	DESC:In a number of cities equal to her Charisma bonus (%1) the urban druid needs only half an hour for a Gather Information check, and may make one as a free action to learn of events of interest (within 1d4 hours, unless her contacts can't reach her).|max(0,CHA)

###Block: Sohei (DMC) Class Features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Sohei (DMC) ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Sohei (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=WeaponProfMartial|TYPE=ArmorProfHeavy	SOURCEPAGE:p.558	DESC:Sohei are proficient with all simple and martial weapons and with all armor, but not with shields.
Ki Frenzy	KEY:Sohei (DMC) ~ Ki Frenzy	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Sohei (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.558	DESC:%1/day (once per encounter, on her own action), the sohei enters a ki frenzy for %2 rounds (3 + Con modifier): +%3 Strength and Dexterity, speed +%4 feet, and a flurry of blows with a full melee attack (one extra attack, -%5 on every attack). She can't use Charisma-, Dexterity- or Intelligence-based skills (except Balance, Escape Artist, Intimidate, Ride), Concentration or patient abilities, cast spells or activate command-word, spell-trigger or spell-completion items, nor use Combat Expertise, item creation or metamagic feats. Afterwards she is fatigued for the encounter (not from 17th level). A nonlawful sohei loses her ki frenzy and spells.|SoheiKiFrenzyUses|3+CON|2+2*(SoheiDMCLVL>=11)+2*(SoheiDMCLVL>=20)|10+10*(SoheiDMCLVL>=11)+10*(SoheiDMCLVL>=20)|2-(SoheiDMCLVL>=11)-(SoheiDMCLVL>=20)
Weapon Focus	KEY:Sohei (DMC) ~ Weapon Focus	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Sohei (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.558	DESC:The sohei gains Weapon Focus with a weapon of her choice as a bonus feat (many choose the naginata).
Deflect Arrows	KEY:Sohei (DMC) ~ Deflect Arrows	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Sohei (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.558	DESC:At 2nd level the sohei gains the Deflect Arrows feat, even without its prerequisite feat and Dexterity.
Diehard	KEY:Sohei (DMC) ~ Diehard	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Sohei (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.558	DESC:At 3rd level the sohei gains the Diehard feat, even without its prerequisite feats.
Spells	KEY:Sohei (DMC) ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Sohei (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.558	DESC:From 4th level the sohei prepares and casts a small number of divine spells from the sohei list like a cleric, choosing freely from the whole list (Wisdom 10 + spell level; DC 10 + spell level + Wis modifier; bonus spells from Wisdom; a 0 means bonus spells only). Caster level: half her sohei level (%1). The Oriental Adventures spells of the list (attraction, weapon bless, warning, castigate, mental strength, discern shapechanger, fatigue, remove fatigue, sustain) are available only with that book.|floor(SoheiDMCLVL/2)
Strength of Mind	KEY:Sohei (DMC) ~ Strength of Mind	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Sohei (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.559	DESC:The sohei is immune to stunning and sleep spells and effects.
Defensive Strike	KEY:Sohei (DMC) ~ Defensive Strike	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Sohei (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.559	DESC:At 6th level the sohei gains the Defensive Strike feat, even without its prerequisite feats and ability scores. (The feat is granted automatically with Oriental Adventures or Complete Warrior, which define it.)
Damage Reduction	KEY:Sohei (DMC) ~ Damage Reduction	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Sohei (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DR:SoheiDR/-	SOURCEPAGE:p.559	DESC:The sohei subtracts %1 from the damage she takes each time she is dealt damage (DR %1/-: 1 at 7th level, +1 at 10th, 13th, 16th and 19th).|SoheiDR
Mettle	KEY:Sohei (DMC) ~ Mettle	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Sohei (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.559	DESC:If the sohei succeeds on a Will or Fortitude save against a spell that would normally reduce its effect ("Will partial", "Fortitude half" and the like), she suffers no effect at all.
Greater Ki Frenzy	KEY:Sohei (DMC) ~ Greater Ki Frenzy	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Sohei (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.559	DESC:During her ki frenzy, the Strength and Dexterity bonuses are +4, the flurry penalty -1 and the speed bonus +20 feet.
Tireless Frenzy	KEY:Sohei (DMC) ~ Tireless Frenzy	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Sohei (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.559	DESC:The sohei is no longer fatigued at the end of her ki frenzy.
Whirlwind Frenzy	KEY:Sohei (DMC) ~ Whirlwind Frenzy	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Sohei (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.559	DESC:During her ki frenzy, the Strength and Dexterity bonuses are +6, there is no flurry penalty and the speed bonus is +30 feet.

###Block: Shaman (DMC) Class Features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Shaman (DMC) ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Shaman (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=WeaponProfSimple|TYPE=ArmorProfLight	SOURCEPAGE:p.549	DESC:Shamans are proficient with all simple weapons and with light armor.
Spells	KEY:Shaman (DMC) ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Shaman (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.550	DESC:The shaman prepares and casts divine spells from the whole shaman spell list (Wisdom 10 + spell level; DC 10 + spell level + Wis modifier; bonus spells from Wisdom), praying for an hour each day at a chosen time. He can't cast spells of an alignment opposed to his own. Spells existing only in other books (Oriental Adventures, Complete Arcane, Spell Compendium, ...) are on his list when such a book is loaded.
Domains	KEY:Shaman (DMC) ~ Domains	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Shaman (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.550	DESC:The shaman chooses two domains from the shaman domains (Ancestor, Celestial, Community, Divination, Flame, Fortune, Fury, Grave, Guardian, Hero, Knowledge, Metal, Nature, River, Stone, Travel, Trickery, War, Wood), a third at 11th level (%1 now). He gains their granted powers and one domain spell slot per spell level for a spell of his domains; from 11th level some levels get a second domain slot (here an additional slot of that level). Domain spells not on the shaman list can be prepared only in the domain slot.|ShamanDMCDomainCount
Spontaneous Casting	KEY:Shaman (DMC) ~ Spontaneous Casting	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Shaman (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.550	DESC:A good shaman can lose a prepared spell (not a domain spell) to cast a cure spell of the same level or lower, an evil shaman an inflict spell; a neutral shaman chooses one of the two once (which also decides turning or rebuking).
Unarmed Strike	KEY:Shaman (DMC) ~ Unarmed Strike	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Shaman (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Improved Unarmed Strike	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|Monk ~ Unarmed Damage	DEFINE:MonkUnarmedDamageLVL|0	BONUS:VAR|MonkUnarmedDamageLVL|1+3*(ShamanDMCLVL>=6)+4*(ShamanDMCLVL>=12)+4*(ShamanDMCLVL>=18)	SOURCEPAGE:p.550	DESC:Like monks, shamans fight unarmed: Improved Unarmed Strike as a bonus feat and unarmed damage of 1d6 (Medium) at 1st level, 1d8 at 6th, 1d10 at 12th, 2d6 at 18th (Small: 1d4/1d6/1d8/1d10; Large: 1d8/1d10/2d6/2d8 - here computed with the monk's size table).
Animal Companion	KEY:Shaman (DMC) ~ Animal Companion	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Shaman (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Animal Companion	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|DMC ~ Animal Companion Alternate	BONUS:VAR|AnimalCompanionLVL|ShamanDMCLVL	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Badger,Camel,Dire Animal (Dire Rat),Dog,Dog (Riding),Eagle,Hawk,Horse (Light),Horse (Heavy),Owl,Pony,Snake (Viper/Small),Snake (Viper/Medium),Wolf,Crocodile,Porpoise,Shark (Medium),Squid	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Ape,Companion ~ Bear (Black),Companion ~ Bison,Companion ~ Boar,Companion ~ Cheetah,Companion ~ Crocodile,Companion ~ Leopard,Companion ~ Lizard (Monitor),Companion ~ Shark (Large),Companion ~ Snake (Constrictor),Companion ~ Snake (Viper/Large),Companion ~ Wolverine|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-3	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Bear (Brown),Companion ~ Crocodile (Giant),Companion ~ Lion,Companion ~ Rhinoceros,Companion ~ Snake (Viper/Huge),Companion ~ Tiger|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-6	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Bear (Polar),Companion ~ Shark (Huge),Companion ~ Snake (Constrictor/Giant),Companion ~ Whale (Orca)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-9	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Elephant,Companion ~ Octopus (Giant)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-12	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Squid (Giant)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-15	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Badger),Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Bat),Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Weasel)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-3	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Dinosaur (Deinonychus),Companion ~ Dinosaur (Elasmosaurus),Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Ape),Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Boar),Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Wolf),Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Wolverine)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-6	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Dinosaur (Megaraptor),Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Lion)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-9	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Bear)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-12	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Dinosaur (Triceratops),Companion ~ Dinosaur (Tyrannosaurus),Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Shark),Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Tiger)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-15	SOURCEPAGE:p.550	DESC:Like a druid, the shaman has an animal companion (badger, camel, dire rat, dog, riding dog, eagle, hawk, light or heavy horse, owl, pony, Small or Medium viper, wolf; in aquatic campaigns crocodile, porpoise, Medium shark, squid), advancing with his shaman level as a druid's; from 4th level also the druid's alternative lists.
Spirit Sight	KEY:Shaman (DMC) ~ Spirit Sight	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Shaman (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.551	DESC:The shaman sees ethereal creatures (including spirits) as easily as material ones, and can tell them apart (they appear translucent).
Turn or Rebuke Undead	KEY:Shaman (DMC) ~ Turn or Rebuke Undead	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Shaman (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Basic Turning	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Turn Undead|1|TYPE=ClassFeature	BONUS:VAR|TurnLevelBase,TurnDamagePlusBase|ShamanDMCLVL-2	BONUS:VAR|TurnTimesBase|3+CHA|TYPE=Base	BONUS:VAR|TurnCheckBase|CHA|TYPE=Base	SOURCEPAGE:p.551	DESC:The shaman turns or rebukes undead as a cleric two levels lower (%1), 3 + Charisma modifier times per day; a neutral shaman chooses (see spontaneous casting). Extra Turning adds four uses each time.|ShamanDMCLVL-2
Bonus Feat	KEY:Shaman (DMC) ~ Bonus Feat	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Shaman (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.551	DESC:At 4th level and every four levels after, the shaman gains a bonus martial arts feat from: Blind-Fight, Combat Reflexes, Falling Star Strike, Freezing the Lifeblood, Great Ki Shout, Iron Will, Ki Shout, Pain Touch, Stunning Fist, Unbalancing Strike (meeting the prerequisites). Falling Star Strike, Great Ki Shout, Ki Shout and Unbalancing Strike exist with Oriental Adventures, Freezing the Lifeblood and Pain Touch with Oriental Adventures or Complete Warrior.
Spirits' Favor	KEY:Shaman (DMC) ~ Spirits' Favor	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Shaman (DMC) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SAVE|ALL|MAX(CHA,0)	SOURCEPAGE:p.551	DESC:The shaman applies his Charisma modifier (if positive) as a bonus on all saving throws.

###Block: Shaman (DMC) domain granted powers
Ancestor (Shaman)	KEY:Ancestor (Shaman)	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:Oriental Adventures	DESC:A number of times per day equal to your Charisma bonus (minimum once), you can summon an ancestor and channel some of its karmic power: a +4 insight bonus on any skill check.
Celestial (Shaman)	KEY:Celestial (Shaman)	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:Oriental Adventures	DESC:Rebuke or command spirits as an evil cleric rebukes undead, a number of times per day equal to 1 + your Charisma modifier.
Community (Shaman)	KEY:Community (Shaman)	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain.SpecialQuality	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=1|CASTERLEVEL=ShamanDMCLVL|Calm Emotions	BONUS:SKILL|Diplomacy|2|TYPE=Competence	SOURCEPAGE:Oriental Adventures	DESC:Use calm emotions as a spell-like ability once per day; +2 competence bonus on Diplomacy checks.
Divination (Shaman)	KEY:Divination (Shaman)	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:Oriental Adventures	DESC:You cast divination spells at +2 caster level.
Flame (Shaman)	KEY:Flame (Shaman)	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:Oriental Adventures	DESC:Flame ward, once per day (spell-like, standard action, abjuration): you or a creature touched gains a resistance bonus equal to your shaman level on saves against fire spells and effects for 1 minute + 1 minute/level.
Fortune (Shaman)	KEY:Fortune (Shaman)	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:Oriental Adventures	DESC:Good fortune, once per day (extraordinary): reroll one roll you have just made; you must take the reroll.
Fury (Shaman)	KEY:Fury (Shaman)	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:Oriental Adventures	DESC:Smite, once per day (supernatural): a single melee attack with a +4 attack bonus and a damage bonus equal to your shaman level; declare before the attack.
Grave (Shaman)	KEY:Grave (Shaman)	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:Oriental Adventures	DESC:Death touch, once per day (spell-like, death effect): on a melee touch attack against a living creature roll 1d6 per shaman level; if the total at least equals its current hit points, it dies.
Guardian (Shaman)	KEY:Guardian (Shaman)	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:Oriental Adventures	DESC:Once per day, you can add your shaman level to a single saving throw you make.
Hero (Shaman)	KEY:Hero (Shaman)	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:Oriental Adventures	DESC:Once per day, you can add your shaman level to a single attack roll.
Knowledge (Shaman)	KEY:Knowledge (Shaman)	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:Oriental Adventures	DESC:All Knowledge skills are class skills. You cast divinations at +1 caster level.
Metal (Shaman)	KEY:Metal (Shaman)	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:Oriental Adventures	DESC:Metal ward, once per day (spell-like, standard action, abjuration): you or a creature touched gains damage reduction 1/- against attacks from metal weapons or spell effects for 1 minute + 1 minute/level.
Nature (Shaman)	KEY:Nature (Shaman)	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:Oriental Adventures	DESC:Rebuke or command normal animals or plant creatures as an evil cleric rebukes or commands undead, 3 + Charisma modifier times per day.
River (Shaman)	KEY:River (Shaman)	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:Oriental Adventures	DESC:Swim speed 30 feet (no water breathing); no Swim checks to swim normally; +8 on Swim checks for special actions or hazards, can always take 10 on them; can run while swimming in a straight line.
Stone (Shaman)	KEY:Stone (Shaman)	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:Oriental Adventures	DESC:Stone ward, once per day (spell-like, standard action, abjuration): you or a creature touched gains damage reduction 5/- against stone weapons, stone creatures (earth elementals, gargoyles, clay and stone golems), spell effects, or falling onto earth or stone, for 1 minute + 1 minute/level.
Travel (Shaman)	KEY:Travel (Shaman)	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:Oriental Adventures	DESC:For a total of 1 round per shaman level per day, you act normally regardless of magical effects that impede movement (as freedom of movement; supernatural, automatic). Survival is a class skill.
Trickery (Shaman)	KEY:Trickery (Shaman)	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:Oriental Adventures	DESC:Bluff, Disguise and Hide are class skills.
War (Shaman)	KEY:War (Shaman)	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain.SpecialQuality	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Weapon Focus|1	SOURCEPAGE:Oriental Adventures	DESC:Free Martial Weapon Proficiency (if necessary) and Weapon Focus with a Small or Medium simple or martial melee weapon of your choice.
Wood (Shaman)	KEY:Wood (Shaman)	CATEGORY:Domain	TYPE:Domain.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:Oriental Adventures	DESC:Move through natural thorns, briars, overgrown areas and similar terrain at normal speed without damage or impairment (magically manipulated terrain still impedes).

###Block: Gen traits (sha'ir familiars)
Air Mastery	KEY:Gen ~ Air Mastery	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.539	DESC:An airborne creature takes a -1 penalty on attack and damage rolls against an air gen.
Earth Mastery	KEY:Gen ~ Earth Mastery	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.539	DESC:An earth gen gains a +1 bonus on attack and damage rolls if both it and its foe are touching the ground; if the opponent is airborne or waterborne, the gen takes a -4 penalty on attack and damage rolls.
Heat	KEY:Gen ~ Heat	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.539	DESC:A fire gen's red-hot body deals 1 point of extra fire damage whenever it hits in melee, or in each round it maintains a hold while grappling.
Amphibious	KEY:Gen ~ Amphibious	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.539	DESC:Although water gens are aquatic, they can survive indefinitely on land.
Elemental Endurance	KEY:Gen ~ Elemental Endurance	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.539	DESC:A gen survives on the elemental planes like a native: immune to fire damage on the Plane of Fire; breathes water and has a swim speed equal to its fly speed (with the +8 racial bonus on Swim checks) on the Plane of Water; a burrow speed equal to its land speed, leaving no trace (as a xorn's earth glide), on the Plane of Earth.
Fetch Spells	KEY:Gen ~ Fetch Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.539	DESC:A gen can find and deliver spells to a sha'ir from the elemental planes; the time required depends on the spell (see the sha'ir).
Elemental Travel	KEY:Gen ~ Elemental Travel	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.539	DESC:A gen can plane shift at will to any elemental plane or from an elemental plane to the Material Plane, transporting only itself (caster level 13th).

###Block: Undead minion traits (death master)
Turn Resistance	KEY:Undead Minion ~ Turn Resistance	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.187	DESC:The undead minion gains turn resistance +4, in addition to any turn resistance it normally has.
Unholy Might	KEY:Undead Minion ~ Unholy Might	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.187	DESC:Once per day as a standard action, the death master can touch his minion to imbue it with unholy energy: +4 Strength and +2 on all saves for 5 + the death master's Charisma modifier rounds.
Persistent Corruption	KEY:Undead Minion ~ Persistent Corruption	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.187	DESC:If the minion is destroyed, Orcus returns a replacement after only 1 hour (24 hours if the death master dismissed it).
Link of the Grave	KEY:Undead Minion ~ Link of the Grave	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.187	DESC:Once per day as a free action, the death master can link himself to his minion as a reversed shield other (caster level = death master level): the minion takes half the damage dealt to him.
Relentless Undead	KEY:Undead Minion ~ Relentless Undead	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:FastHealing|0	BONUS:VAR|FastHealing|3	SOURCEPAGE:p.187	DESC:The minion gains fast healing 3.

###Block: Hiveblood Creature and Savage Creature template abilities
Limited Hive Mind	KEY:Hiveblood Creature ~ Limited Hive Mind	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.1529	DESC:Hiveblood creatures within a distance of their queen are in constant communication (the distance is missing in the compendium's print; a formian's own hive mind reaches 50 miles). If one is aware of a particular danger, they all are; if one in a group is not flat-footed, none of them are; no hiveblood in a group is considered flanked unless they all are.
Death Throes	KEY:Savage Creature ~ Death Throes	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.1553	DESC:When a savage creature dies, it can immediately make a free bite attack against one creature in reach. Then its body melts into acidic goo, leaving only its gear and skeleton: any living creature within 5 feet takes 1d6 points of acid damage (Reflex DC 15 negates; living flesh only). The acid pool remains for a minute, then dries to harmless green powder.
Disease	KEY:Savage Creature ~ Disease	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.1553	DESC:A creature bitten by a savage creature must make a Fortitude save (DC 10 + 1/2 the savage creature's racial HD + its Con modifier) or contract savage fever: incubation 1 minute, then 1d6 points of Intelligence damage and another save each day against a further 1d6. At Intelligence 0 the victim falls into a coma and transforms into a savage creature; its Intelligence then heals to its new maximum and it seeks fresh prey.
Afflicted	KEY:Savage Creature ~ Afflicted	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.1553	DESC:A greater restoration reverts a savage creature to normal if the caster succeeds on a caster level check (DC 10 + 1/2 the savage creature's HD + its Charisma modifier); miracle or wish restores it automatically. A savage creature killed and brought back to life loses the template.
Ferocity	KEY:Savage Creature ~ Ferocity	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.1553	DESC:A savage creature fights without penalty while disabled and dying.
Immunities	KEY:Savage Creature ~ Immunities	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.1553	DESC:A savage creature is immune to disease, exhaustion, fatigue, mind-affecting effects, stunning and pain-related effects.

###Block: Anarch class features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Anarch ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Internal	TYPE:Internal	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=WeaponProfMartial|TYPE=ArmorProfHeavy|TYPE=ShieldProf	SOURCEPAGE:p.405	DESC:Proficient with all simple and martial weapons, all types of armor and shields (except tower shields).
Aura of Chaos	KEY:Anarch ~ Aura of Chaos	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Anarch Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.405	DESC:The power of the anarch's aura of chaos (see the detect chaos spell) is equal to his anarch level (%1).|AnarchLVL
Detect Law	KEY:Anarch ~ Detect Law	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Anarch Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=ATWILL|CASTERLEVEL=AnarchLVL|Detect Law	SOURCEPAGE:p.405	DESC:At will, the anarch can use detect law, as the spell.
Smite Law	KEY:Anarch ~ Smite Law	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Anarch Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.405	DESC:%1/day, the anarch may attempt to smite law with one normal melee attack: he adds his Charisma bonus (if any) to the attack roll and deals 1 extra point of damage per anarch level (+%2). Smiting a creature that is not lawful has no effect, but the use is expended.|AnarchSmite|AnarchLVL
Divine Grace	KEY:Anarch ~ Divine Grace	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Anarch Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SAVE|ALL|MAX(CHA,0)	SOURCEPAGE:p.405	DESC:The anarch gains a bonus equal to his Charisma bonus (if any) on all saving throws.
Destructive Strike	KEY:Anarch ~ Destructive Strike	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Anarch Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.405	DESC:A number of times per day equal to his Charisma modifier (%1), the anarch can deal critical hit damage (not sneak attack damage) to an object or construct with a melee attack; he decides after a critical hit is rolled, before the confirmation roll (a failed confirmation wastes the use).|max(0,CHA)
Aura of Courage	KEY:Anarch ~ Aura of Courage	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Anarch Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.405	DESC:The anarch is immune to fear (magical or otherwise); each ally within 10 feet gains a +4 morale bonus on saving throws against fear effects (not while he is unconscious or dead).
Slippery Mind	KEY:Anarch ~ Slippery Mind	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Anarch Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.405	DESC:If the anarch is affected by an enchantment spell or effect and fails his saving throw, he can attempt it again 1 round later to break free (only one extra save).
Turn Construct	KEY:Anarch ~ Turn Construct	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Anarch Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.405	DESC:The anarch can turn or destroy constructs %1 times per day (3 + Charisma modifier), as a cleric three levels lower (%2) turns undead.|3+CHA|AnarchLVL-3
Spells	KEY:Anarch ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Anarch Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.405	DESC:From 4th level the anarch prepares and casts divine spells from the anarch spell list like a paladin (Wisdom 10 + spell level; DC 10 + spell level + Wis modifier; bonus spells from Wisdom; a 0 means bonus spells only); caster level half his anarch level.
Special Mount	KEY:Anarch ~ Special Mount	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Anarch Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Special Mount	BONUS:VAR|SpecialMountLVL|AnarchLVL	SOURCEPAGE:p.405	DESC:The anarch gains a special mount, just as a paladin does.
Dispel Law	KEY:Anarch ~ Dispel Law	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Anarch Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=AnarchDispel|TIMEUNIT=Week|CASTERLEVEL=AnarchLVL|Dispel Law	SOURCEPAGE:p.405	DESC:The anarch can use dispel law, as the spell, %1 times per week (once at 8th level, one more every four levels); caster level = anarch level.|AnarchDispel
Code of Conduct	KEY:Anarch ~ Code of Conduct	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Anarch Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.405	DESC:An anarch must be chaotic neutral and loses all class abilities if he ever willingly commits a blatantly lawful act (abiding by an oath, fulfilling a contract, joining an organization). He never knowingly associates with lawful characters and accepts only chaotic neutral henchmen, familiars, followers or cohorts.

###Block: Anti-Paladin class features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Anti-Paladin ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Internal	TYPE:Internal	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=WeaponProfMartial|TYPE=ArmorProfHeavy|TYPE=ShieldProf	SOURCEPAGE:p.407	DESC:Proficient with all simple and martial weapons, all types of armor and shields (except tower shields).
Aura of Evil	KEY:Anti-Paladin ~ Aura of Evil	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Anti-Paladin Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.407	DESC:The power of the anti-paladin's aura of evil (see the detect evil spell) is equal to his anti-paladin level (%1).|AntiPaladinLVL
Detect Good	KEY:Anti-Paladin ~ Detect Good	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Anti-Paladin Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=ATWILL|CASTERLEVEL=AntiPaladinLVL|Detect Good	SOURCEPAGE:p.407	DESC:At will, the anti-paladin can use detect good, as the spell.
Smite Good	KEY:Anti-Paladin ~ Smite Good	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Anti-Paladin Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.407	DESC:%1/day, the anti-paladin may attempt to smite good with one normal melee attack: he adds his Charisma bonus (if any) to the attack roll and deals 1 extra point of damage per anti-paladin level (+%2). Smiting a creature that is not good has no effect, but the use is expended.|AntiPaladinSmite|AntiPaladinLVL
Divine Grace	KEY:Anti-Paladin ~ Divine Grace	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Anti-Paladin Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SAVE|ALL|MAX(CHA,0)	SOURCEPAGE:p.407	DESC:The anti-paladin gains a bonus equal to his Charisma bonus (if any) on all saving throws.
Slaughter the Weak	KEY:Anti-Paladin ~ Slaughter the Weak	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Anti-Paladin Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.407	DESC:The anti-paladin gains a +2 morale bonus on melee attack and damage rolls against any creature with fewer Hit Dice than he has; dying creatures with fewer Hit Dice take a -2 penalty on saves against his death knell.
Aura of Fear	KEY:Anti-Paladin ~ Aura of Fear	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Anti-Paladin Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.407	DESC:Each enemy within 10 feet takes a -4 morale penalty on saving throws against fear effects; the anti-paladin is immune to fear. Not while he is unconscious or dead; he can suppress or activate the aura as a free action.
Death Knell	KEY:Anti-Paladin ~ Death Knell	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Anti-Paladin Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=AntiPaladinDeathKnell|CASTERLEVEL=AntiPaladinLVL|Death Knell	SOURCEPAGE:p.407	DESC:The anti-paladin can cast death knell, as the spell, %1/day (once at 3rd level, one more every five levels); caster level = anti-paladin level.|AntiPaladinDeathKnell
Turn or Rebuke Outsider	KEY:Anti-Paladin ~ Turn or Rebuke Outsider	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Anti-Paladin Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.407	DESC:The anti-paladin can turn or destroy good outsiders, or rebuke or command evil outsiders, %1 times per day (3 + Charisma modifier), as a cleric three levels lower (%2) turns undead.|3+CHA|AntiPaladinLVL-3
Spells	KEY:Anti-Paladin ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Anti-Paladin Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.407	DESC:From 4th level the anti-paladin prepares and casts divine spells from the anti-paladin spell list like a paladin (Wisdom 10 + spell level; DC 10 + spell level + Wis modifier; bonus spells from Wisdom; a 0 means bonus spells only); caster level half his anti-paladin level.
Fiendish Mount	KEY:Anti-Paladin ~ Fiendish Mount	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Anti-Paladin Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Special Mount	BONUS:VAR|SpecialMountLVL|AntiPaladinLVL	SOURCEPAGE:p.407	DESC:The anti-paladin gains a special mount as a paladin does, except that it always has the fiendish template and remains for 1 hour per anti-paladin level once called.
Contagion	KEY:Anti-Paladin ~ Contagion	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Anti-Paladin Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=AntiPaladinContagion|TIMEUNIT=Week|CASTERLEVEL=AntiPaladinLVL|Contagion	SOURCEPAGE:p.407	DESC:The anti-paladin can cast contagion, as the spell, %1 times per week (once at 6th level, one more every three levels); caster level = anti-paladin level.|AntiPaladinContagion
Code of Conduct	KEY:Anti-Paladin ~ Code of Conduct	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Anti-Paladin Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.407	DESC:An anti-paladin must be chaotic evil and loses all class abilities if he ever willingly commits a good act. He works to undermine civilization and good peoples, never offers mercy or quarter unless he betrays his word within the hour, joins no organization (services only for pay, leading to chaos). He adventures with any non-good characters but never knowingly with good ones, and accepts only chaotic evil henchmen, followers or cohorts (always the -2 cruelty penalty on Leadership).

###Block: Avenger class features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Avenger ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Internal	TYPE:Internal	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=WeaponProfMartial|TYPE=ArmorProfHeavy|TYPE=ShieldProf	SOURCEPAGE:p.409	DESC:Proficient with all simple and martial weapons, all types of armor and shields (except tower shields).
Aura of Chaos	KEY:Avenger ~ Aura of Chaos	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Avenger Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.409	DESC:The power of the avenger's aura of chaos (see the detect chaos spell) is equal to her avenger level (%1).|AvengerLVL
Detect Law	KEY:Avenger ~ Detect Law	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Avenger Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=ATWILL|CASTERLEVEL=AvengerLVL|Detect Law	SOURCEPAGE:p.409	DESC:At will, the avenger can use detect law, as the spell.
Smite Law	KEY:Avenger ~ Smite Law	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Avenger Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.409	DESC:%1/day, the avenger may attempt to smite law with one normal melee attack: she adds her Charisma bonus (if any) to the attack roll and deals 1 extra point of damage per avenger level (+%2). Smiting a creature that is not lawful has no effect, but the use is expended.|AvengerSmite|AvengerLVL
Divine Grace	KEY:Avenger ~ Divine Grace	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Avenger Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SAVE|ALL|MAX(CHA,0)	SOURCEPAGE:p.409	DESC:The avenger gains a bonus equal to her Charisma bonus (if any) on all saving throws.
Lay on Hands	KEY:Avenger ~ Lay on Hands	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Avenger Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.409	DESC:With Charisma 12 or higher, the avenger can heal %1 hit points of damage per day (avenger level x Charisma bonus) by touch, divided as she wishes (standard action), or use them to damage undead with a melee touch attack, as the paladin ability.|AvengerLVL*MAX(CHA,0)
Aura of Courage	KEY:Avenger ~ Aura of Courage	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Avenger Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.409	DESC:The avenger is immune to fear (magical or otherwise); each ally within 10 feet gains a +4 morale bonus on saving throws against fear effects (not while she is unconscious or dead).
Slippery Mind	KEY:Avenger ~ Slippery Mind	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Avenger Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.409	DESC:If the avenger is affected by an enchantment spell or effect and fails her saving throw, she can attempt it again 1 round later to break free (only one extra save).
Turn Undead	KEY:Avenger ~ Turn Undead	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Avenger Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.409	DESC:The avenger turns undead just like a paladin: %1 times per day (3 + Charisma modifier), as a cleric three levels lower (%2).|3+CHA|AvengerLVL-3
Spells	KEY:Avenger ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Avenger Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.409	DESC:From 4th level the avenger prepares and casts divine spells from the avenger spell list like a paladin (Wisdom 10 + spell level; DC 10 + spell level + Wis modifier; bonus spells from Wisdom; a 0 means bonus spells only); caster level half her avenger level. (The list gives cure moderate wounds at 2nd and 3rd level - kept at 2nd.)
Animal Minion	KEY:Avenger ~ Animal Minion	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Avenger Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	FOLLOWERS:Special Mount|1	DEFINE:SpecialMountLVL|0	BONUS:VAR|SpecialMountLVL|AvengerLVL	COMPANIONLIST:Special Mount|RACETYPE=Animal	SOURCEPAGE:p.409	DESC:The avenger gains an animal minion - a scout, combatant or guardian, usually a bird - of her size or smaller, never used as a mount. It is otherwise treated as a paladin's special mount in all ways, including the abilities it gains with her levels and the repercussions if it is lost. (The size limit is not enforced: choose an animal no larger than the avenger.)
Break Enchantment	KEY:Avenger ~ Break Enchantment	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Avenger Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=AvengerBreak|TIMEUNIT=Week|CASTERLEVEL=AvengerLVL|Break Enchantment	SOURCEPAGE:p.409	DESC:The avenger can use break enchantment as a spell-like ability %1 times per week (once at 6th level, one more every three levels).|AvengerBreak
Code of Conduct	KEY:Avenger ~ Code of Conduct	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Avenger Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.409	DESC:An avenger must be chaotic good and loses all class abilities if she ever willingly commits an evil act or willingly allies with a lawful government or affiliated agency. She tempers vengeance (killing is the last resort, reserved for the most evil villains), aids anyone who asks for help (within reason) and joins no organized association, order or group. She adventures with good or neutral characters (lawful ones only for a limited time), never knowingly with evil ones, and accepts only chaotic good henchmen, followers or cohorts.

###Block: Corrupter class features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Corrupter ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Internal	TYPE:Internal	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=WeaponProfMartial|TYPE=ArmorProfHeavy|TYPE=ShieldProf	SOURCEPAGE:p.413	DESC:Proficient with all simple and martial weapons, all types of armor and shields (except tower shields).
Aura of Evil	KEY:Corrupter ~ Aura of Evil	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Corrupter Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.413	DESC:The power of the corrupter's aura of evil (see the detect evil spell) is equal to his corrupter level (%1).|CorrupterLVL
Detect Good	KEY:Corrupter ~ Detect Good	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Corrupter Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=ATWILL|CASTERLEVEL=CorrupterLVL|Detect Good	SOURCEPAGE:p.413	DESC:At will, the corrupter can use detect good, as the spell.
Smite Heathen	KEY:Corrupter ~ Smite Heathen	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Corrupter Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.413	DESC:%1/day, the corrupter may smite a creature able (or potentially able, like a paladin or ranger below 4th level) to cast divine spells, except worshipers of his own faith: one normal melee attack adding his Charisma bonus (if any) to the attack roll and 1 extra point of damage per corrupter level (+%2). Smiting any other creature has no effect, but the use is expended.|CorrupterSmite|CorrupterLVL
Divine Grace	KEY:Corrupter ~ Divine Grace	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Corrupter Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SAVE|ALL|MAX(CHA,0)	SOURCEPAGE:p.413	DESC:The corrupter gains a bonus equal to his Charisma bonus (if any) on all saving throws.
Hidden Faith	KEY:Corrupter ~ Hidden Faith	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Corrupter Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.413	DESC:The corrupter's faith is hidden: a +4 profane bonus on Bluff, Disguise and Forgery checks to maintain the deception, and any magical attempt to discern his actual faith fails unless the caster succeeds on a level check (DC %1 = corrupter level + 10).|CorrupterLVL+10
Aura of Fear	KEY:Corrupter ~ Aura of Fear	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Corrupter Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.413	DESC:Each enemy within 10 feet takes a -4 morale penalty on saving throws against fear effects; the corrupter is immune to fear. Not while he is unconscious or dead; he can suppress or activate the aura as a free action.
Disguise Self	KEY:Corrupter ~ Disguise Self	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Corrupter Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=max(1,CHA)|CASTERLEVEL=CorrupterLVL|Disguise Self	SOURCEPAGE:p.413	DESC:The corrupter can cast disguise self, as the spell, %1/day (his Charisma bonus, minimum once); caster level = corrupter level.|max(1,CHA)
Intercession	KEY:Corrupter ~ Intercession	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Corrupter Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.413	DESC:%1 times per day (3 + Charisma modifier), the corrupter makes a turning check as a cleric three levels lower (%2): the result is the highest-level divine spellcaster he can cut off from her deity, the turning damage the maximum total Hit Dice of divine spellcasters within 60 feet affected (closest first). They can't cast divine spells for 1 minute - for 24 hours if his corrupter level is at least twice their divine spellcaster level - until he attacks them or they receive atonement.|3+CHA|CorrupterLVL-3
Spells	KEY:Corrupter ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Corrupter Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.413	DESC:From 4th level the corrupter prepares and casts divine spells from the corrupter spell list like a paladin (Wisdom 10 + spell level; DC 10 + spell level + Wis modifier; bonus spells from Wisdom; a 0 means bonus spells only); caster level half his corrupter level.
Fiendish Familiar	KEY:Corrupter ~ Fiendish Familiar	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Corrupter Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Improved Familiar	FOLLOWERS:Familiar|1	DEFINE:FamiliarLVL|0	BONUS:VAR|FamiliarLVL|CorrupterLVL	COMPANIONLIST:Familiar|Companion ~ Devil (Imp),Companion ~ Demon (Quasit)	SOURCEPAGE:p.413	DESC:The corrupter gains Improved Familiar as a bonus feat (even without its prerequisites); his familiar must be an imp or a quasit and uses his corrupter level as the master class level. (PCGen keeps the core rules' alignment condition on the imp - lawful evil, lawful neutral or chaotic evil masters - so a neutral evil corrupter is offered only the quasit; add the imp by hand if wanted.)
Fallen Soul	KEY:Corrupter ~ Fallen Soul	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Corrupter Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=CorrupterFallen|TIMEUNIT=Week|CASTERLEVEL=CorrupterLVL|Fallen Soul	SOURCEPAGE:p.413	DESC:The corrupter can cast fallen soul, as the spell, %1 times per week (once at 8th level, one more every four levels).|CorrupterFallen
Code of Conduct	KEY:Corrupter ~ Code of Conduct	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Corrupter Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.413	DESC:A corrupter must be neutral evil and loses all class abilities if he ever willingly commits a good act or an act that exposes his faith to an opposing religion to his detriment. He strives to corrupt all other faiths (good ones above all), may make any vows needed to keep his deception as long as he prays privately to his deity an hour each day, and must remain hidden. He adventures with any alignment (good ones only while secretly converting them) and accepts only evil henchmen, followers or cohorts.

###Block: Despot class features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Despot ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Internal	TYPE:Internal	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=WeaponProfMartial|TYPE=ArmorProfHeavy|TYPE=ShieldProf	SOURCEPAGE:p.417	DESC:Proficient with all simple and martial weapons, all types of armor and shields (except tower shields).
Aura of Law	KEY:Despot ~ Aura of Law	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Despot Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.417	DESC:The power of the despot's aura of law (see the detect law spell) is equal to her despot level (%1).|DespotLVL
Detect Chaos	KEY:Despot ~ Detect Chaos	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Despot Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=ATWILL|CASTERLEVEL=DespotLVL|Detect Chaos	SOURCEPAGE:p.417	DESC:At will, the despot can use detect chaos, as the spell.
Smite Chaos	KEY:Despot ~ Smite Chaos	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Despot Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.417	DESC:%1/day, the despot may attempt to smite chaos with one normal melee attack: she adds her Charisma bonus (if any) to the attack roll and deals 1 extra point of damage per despot level (+%2). Smiting a creature that is not chaotic has no effect, but the use is expended.|DespotSmite|DespotLVL
Divine Grace	KEY:Despot ~ Divine Grace	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Despot Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SAVE|ALL|MAX(CHA,0)	SOURCEPAGE:p.417	DESC:The despot gains a bonus equal to her Charisma bonus (if any) on all saving throws.
Slippery Mind	KEY:Despot ~ Slippery Mind	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Despot Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.417	DESC:If the despot is affected by an enchantment spell or effect and fails her saving throw, she can attempt it again 1 round later to break free (only one extra save).
Aura of Fear	KEY:Despot ~ Aura of Fear	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Despot Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.417	DESC:Each enemy within 10 feet takes a -4 morale penalty on saving throws against fear effects; the despot is immune to fear. Not while she is unconscious or dead; she can suppress or activate the aura as a free action.
Indomitable Will	KEY:Despot ~ Indomitable Will	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Despot Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.417	DESC:The despot is completely immune to all spells of the charm subschool.
Oppression	KEY:Despot ~ Oppression	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Despot Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.417	DESC:%1 times per day (3 + Charisma modifier), the despot oppresses living creatures within 60 feet that understand her (language-dependent, mind-affecting): a turning check (1d20 + Cha modifier) as a cleric three levels lower (%2) gives how many targets, the turning damage their total Hit Dice (chaotic creatures first, lawful last; closer ones first). Oppressed targets are sickened (-2 on attack rolls, weapon damage, saves, skill and ability checks) for 1 minute; nauseated instead if she has at least twice their levels.|3+CHA|DespotLVL-3
Spells	KEY:Despot ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Despot Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.417	DESC:From 4th level the despot prepares and casts divine spells from the despot spell list like a paladin (Wisdom 10 + spell level; DC 10 + spell level + Wis modifier; bonus spells from Wisdom; a 0 means bonus spells only); caster level half her despot level.
Leadership	KEY:Despot ~ Leadership	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Despot Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Leadership	BONUS:VAR|LeadershipScore|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.417	DESC:The despot gains Leadership as a bonus feat and a +1 bonus to her Leadership score.
Mark of Justice	KEY:Despot ~ Mark of Justice	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Despot Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=DespotMark|TIMEUNIT=Week|CASTERLEVEL=DespotLVL|Mark of Justice	SOURCEPAGE:p.417	DESC:The despot can cast mark of justice, as the spell, %1 times per week (once at 7th level, one more every four levels, 4 at 19th).|DespotMark
Code of Conduct	KEY:Despot ~ Code of Conduct	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Despot Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.417	DESC:A despot must be lawful evil and loses all class abilities if she ever willingly commits a chaotic act (breaking a vow or contract, betraying an ally). She works to expand her domain (by Leadership or by force), may abuse her sovereignty for her own power, but must protect her subjects and allies from other forces and not overburden them. She adventures only with non-chaotic characters (only in groups where she is equal or superior to the highest-level member) and accepts only lawful evil henchmen, followers or cohorts.

###Block: Enforcer class features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Enforcer ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Internal	TYPE:Internal	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=WeaponProfMartial|TYPE=ArmorProfHeavy|TYPE=ShieldProf	SOURCEPAGE:p.423	DESC:Proficient with all simple and martial weapons, all types of armor and shields (except tower shields).
Aura of Law	KEY:Enforcer ~ Aura of Law	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Enforcer Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.423	DESC:The power of the enforcer's aura of law (see the detect law spell) is equal to his enforcer level (%1).|EnforcerLVL
Detect Chaos	KEY:Enforcer ~ Detect Chaos	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Enforcer Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=ATWILL|CASTERLEVEL=EnforcerLVL|Detect Chaos	SOURCEPAGE:p.423	DESC:At will, the enforcer can use detect chaos, as the spell.
Smite Chaos	KEY:Enforcer ~ Smite Chaos	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Enforcer Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.423	DESC:%1/day, the enforcer may attempt to smite chaos with one normal melee attack: he adds his Charisma bonus (if any) to the attack roll and deals 1 extra point of damage per enforcer level (+%2). Smiting a creature that is not chaotic has no effect, but the use is expended.|EnforcerSmite|EnforcerLVL
Divine Grace	KEY:Enforcer ~ Divine Grace	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Enforcer Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SAVE|ALL|MAX(CHA,0)	SOURCEPAGE:p.423	DESC:The enforcer gains a bonus equal to his Charisma bonus (if any) on all saving throws.
Subdue	KEY:Enforcer ~ Subdue	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Enforcer Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.423	DESC:The enforcer takes no -4 penalty on attack rolls to deal nonlethal damage with a weapon he is proficient with that normally deals lethal damage, and gains a +2 bonus on weapon damage rolls when dealing nonlethal damage with a weapon designed for it (such as a sap or whip).
Aura of Courage	KEY:Enforcer ~ Aura of Courage	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Enforcer Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.423	DESC:The enforcer is immune to fear (magical or otherwise); each ally within 10 feet gains a +4 morale bonus on saving throws against fear effects (not while he is unconscious or dead).
Suggestion	KEY:Enforcer ~ Suggestion	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Enforcer Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=EnforcerSuggestion|CASTERLEVEL=EnforcerLVL|Suggestion	SOURCEPAGE:p.423	DESC:The enforcer can cast suggestion, as the spell, %1/day (once at 3rd level, one more at 8th and every five levels after, 4 at 18th); caster level = enforcer level.|EnforcerSuggestion
Rebuke Undead	KEY:Enforcer ~ Rebuke Undead	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Enforcer Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Basic Turning	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Rebuke Undead	BONUS:VAR|TurnLevelBase,TurnDamagePlusBase|EnforcerLVL-3	BONUS:VAR|TurnTimesBase|3+CHA|TYPE=Base	BONUS:VAR|TurnCheckBase|CHA|TYPE=Base	SOURCEPAGE:p.423	DESC:The enforcer rebukes or commands undead as an evil cleric three levels lower (%1), %2 times per day (3 + Charisma modifier); he generally keeps commanded undead no longer than 24 hours, especially where their presence causes chaos in society.|EnforcerLVL-3|3+CHA
Spells	KEY:Enforcer ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Enforcer Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.423	DESC:From 4th level the enforcer prepares and casts divine spells from the enforcer spell list like a paladin (Wisdom 10 + spell level; DC 10 + spell level + Wis modifier; bonus spells from Wisdom; a 0 means bonus spells only); caster level half his enforcer level.
Leadership	KEY:Enforcer ~ Leadership	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Enforcer Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Leadership	BONUS:VAR|LeadershipScore|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.423	DESC:The enforcer gains Leadership as a bonus feat and a +1 bonus to his Leadership score (the maximum number and level of followers and cohorts remain standard).
Dominate Person	KEY:Enforcer ~ Dominate Person	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Enforcer Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=EnforcerDominate|TIMEUNIT=Week|CASTERLEVEL=EnforcerLVL|Dominate Person	SOURCEPAGE:p.423	DESC:The enforcer can cast dominate person, as the spell, %1 times per week (once at 7th level, one more every four levels); caster level = enforcer level.|EnforcerDominate
Code of Conduct	KEY:Enforcer ~ Code of Conduct	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Enforcer Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.423	DESC:An enforcer must be lawful neutral and loses all class abilities if he ever willingly commits a chaotic act (breaking a vow or contract, betraying an ally). He serves his deity and a worldly liege of the same faith (acting against the liege only if he can expose the liege's heresy within 24 hours), never accepts a position without a liege above him (except in an emergency, for at most 24 hours), and upholds the laws of church and land even against his own goals. He adventures with non-chaotic characters and accepts only lawful neutral henchmen, followers or cohorts.

###Block: Incarnate (Paladin) class features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Incarnate (Paladin) ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Internal	TYPE:Internal	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=WeaponProfMartial|TYPE=ArmorProfHeavy|TYPE=ShieldProf	SOURCEPAGE:p.431	DESC:Proficient with all simple and martial weapons, all types of armor and shields (except tower shields).
Detect Imbalance	KEY:Incarnate (Paladin) ~ Detect Imbalance	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Incarnate (Paladin) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.431	DESC:As the detect undead spell, but detecting creatures with an alignment subtype (only their presence, not the alignment or subtype).
Elemental Affinity	KEY:Incarnate (Paladin) ~ Elemental Affinity	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Incarnate (Paladin) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.431	DESC:At 1st level the incarnate chooses an affinity to two elements: air and earth, or fire and water (associated energies: air electricity, earth acid, fire fire, water cold).
Smite Extremist	KEY:Incarnate (Paladin) ~ Smite Extremist	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Incarnate (Paladin) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.431	DESC:%1/day, the incarnate may smite a lawful good, lawful evil, chaotic good or chaotic evil creature (declaring which alignment she smites): one normal melee attack adding her Charisma bonus (if any) to the attack roll and 1 extra point of damage per incarnate level (+%2). Smiting any other creature has no effect, but the use is expended.|IncarnatePaladinSmite|IncarnatePaladinLVL
Divine Grace	KEY:Incarnate (Paladin) ~ Divine Grace	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Incarnate (Paladin) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SAVE|ALL|MAX(CHA,0)	SOURCEPAGE:p.431	DESC:The incarnate gains a bonus equal to her Charisma bonus (if any) on all saving throws.
Elemental Burst	KEY:Incarnate (Paladin) ~ Elemental Burst	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Incarnate (Paladin) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.431	DESC:With Charisma 12 or higher, %1/day (her Charisma bonus) as a standard action, the incarnate directs a burst of energy at a target within 60 feet (ranged touch attack): 1d4+%2 points of damage of each of her two associated energy types.|max(0,CHA)|max(0,CHA)
Aura of Courage	KEY:Incarnate (Paladin) ~ Aura of Courage	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Incarnate (Paladin) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.431	DESC:The incarnate is immune to fear (magical or otherwise); each ally within 10 feet gains a +4 morale bonus on saving throws against fear effects (not while she is unconscious or dead).
Energy Resistance	KEY:Incarnate (Paladin) ~ Energy Resistance	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Incarnate (Paladin) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.431	DESC:The incarnate gains resistance 5 to the two energy types of her elemental affinity (applied by the affinity chosen).
Rebuke Outsider	KEY:Incarnate (Paladin) ~ Rebuke Outsider	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Incarnate (Paladin) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.431	DESC:Only on the Material Plane, the incarnate can rebuke or command outsiders %1 times per day (3 + Charisma modifier), as a cleric three levels lower (%2) turns undead.|3+CHA|IncarnatePaladinLVL-3
Spells	KEY:Incarnate (Paladin) ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Incarnate (Paladin) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.431	DESC:From 4th level the incarnate prepares and casts divine spells from the incarnate spell list like a paladin (Wisdom 10 + spell level; DC 10 + spell level + Wis modifier; bonus spells from Wisdom; a 0 means bonus spells only); caster level half her incarnate level.
Elemental Minion	KEY:Incarnate (Paladin) ~ Elemental Minion	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Incarnate (Paladin) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	FOLLOWERS:Special Mount|1	DEFINE:SpecialMountLVL|0	BONUS:VAR|SpecialMountLVL|IncarnatePaladinLVL	SOURCEPAGE:p.431	DESC:Once a day as a standard action, the incarnate summons a Medium elemental of one of her two affinity elements. It carries the same responsibilities as a paladin's special mount and gains the same bonuses (Hit Dice, natural armor, Strength, Intelligence, special abilities) with her levels, but remains only 1 hour per level.
Commune with Nature	KEY:Incarnate (Paladin) ~ Commune with Nature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Incarnate (Paladin) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=IncarnatePaladinCommune|TIMEUNIT=Week|CASTERLEVEL=IncarnatePaladinLVL|Commune with Nature	SOURCEPAGE:p.431	DESC:The incarnate can use commune with nature, as the spell, %1 times per week (once at 8th level, one more every four levels).|IncarnatePaladinCommune
Code of Conduct	KEY:Incarnate (Paladin) ~ Code of Conduct	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Incarnate (Paladin) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.431	DESC:An incarnate must be neutral and loses all class abilities if she ever willingly commits an act that endangers the natural balance of the world. She serves Balance rather than a deity, avoids other planes (except the elemental planes of her affinity) except in dire need, and prefers peaceful solutions. She adventures with any alignment but distrusts those drawing power from the Outer Planes.
Elemental Affinity (Air and Earth)	KEY:Incarnate (Paladin) ~ Elemental Affinity (Air and Earth)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:IncarnatePaladinElementalAffinity.SpecialQuality	BONUS:VAR|ElectricityResistanceBonus,AcidResistanceBonus|5|PREVARGTEQ:IncarnatePaladinLVL,3	COMPANIONLIST:Special Mount|Elemental (Air Medium),Elemental (Earth Medium)	SOURCEPAGE:p.431	DESC:The incarnate is associated with air (electricity) and earth (acid): her elemental burst deals both energies, she gains resistance 5 to both at 3rd level, and her elemental minion is a Medium air or earth elemental.
Elemental Affinity (Fire and Water)	KEY:Incarnate (Paladin) ~ Elemental Affinity (Fire and Water)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:IncarnatePaladinElementalAffinity.SpecialQuality	BONUS:VAR|FireResistanceBonus,ColdResistanceBonus|5|PREVARGTEQ:IncarnatePaladinLVL,3	COMPANIONLIST:Special Mount|Elemental (Fire Medium),Elemental (Water Medium)	SOURCEPAGE:p.431	DESC:The incarnate is associated with fire (fire) and water (cold): her elemental burst deals both energies, she gains resistance 5 to both at 3rd level, and her elemental minion is a Medium fire or water elemental.

###Block: Sentinel class features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Sentinel ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Internal	TYPE:Internal	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=WeaponProfMartial|TYPE=ArmorProfHeavy|TYPE=ShieldProf	SOURCEPAGE:p.443	DESC:Proficient with all simple and martial weapons, all types of armor and shields (except tower shields).
Aura of Good	KEY:Sentinel ~ Aura of Good	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Sentinel Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.443	DESC:The power of the sentinel's aura of good (see the detect good spell) is equal to his sentinel level (%1), like a cleric of a good deity.|SentinelLVL
Detect Evil	KEY:Sentinel ~ Detect Evil	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Sentinel Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=ATWILL|CASTERLEVEL=SentinelLVL|Detect Evil	SOURCEPAGE:p.443	DESC:At will, the sentinel can use detect evil, as the spell.
Smite Evil	KEY:Sentinel ~ Smite Evil	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Sentinel Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.443	DESC:%1/day, the sentinel may attempt to smite evil with one normal melee attack: he adds his Charisma bonus (if any) to the attack roll and deals 1 extra point of damage per sentinel level (+%2). Smiting a creature that is not evil has no effect, but the use is expended.|SentinelSmite|SentinelLVL
Divine Grace	KEY:Sentinel ~ Divine Grace	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Sentinel Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SAVE|ALL|MAX(CHA,0)	SOURCEPAGE:p.443	DESC:The sentinel gains a bonus equal to his Charisma bonus (if any) on all saving throws.
Resist Fiendish Lure	KEY:Sentinel ~ Resist Fiendish Lure	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Sentinel Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.443	DESC:The sentinel gains a +4 sacred bonus on saving throws against mind-affecting attacks of evil outsiders.
Aura of Courage	KEY:Sentinel ~ Aura of Courage	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Sentinel Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.443	DESC:The sentinel is immune to fear (magical or otherwise); each ally within 10 feet gains a +4 morale bonus on saving throws against fear effects (not while he is unconscious or dead).
Celestial Fortitude	KEY:Sentinel ~ Celestial Fortitude	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Sentinel Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.443	DESC:The sentinel gains a +2 sacred bonus on Fortitude saves against effects from evil outsiders and evil spells; a successful Fortitude save against such an effect that normally deals half damage or a partial effect leaves him unharmed.
Turn Outsider	KEY:Sentinel ~ Turn Outsider	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Sentinel Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.443	DESC:The sentinel can turn or destroy outsiders %1 times per day (3 + Charisma modifier), as a cleric three levels lower (%2) turns undead.|3+CHA|SentinelLVL-3
Spells	KEY:Sentinel ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Sentinel Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.443	DESC:From 4th level the sentinel prepares and casts divine spells from the sentinel spell list like a paladin (Wisdom 10 + spell level; DC 10 + spell level + Wis modifier; bonus spells from Wisdom; a 0 means bonus spells only); caster level half his sentinel level.
Celestial Minion	KEY:Sentinel ~ Celestial Minion	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Sentinel Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	FOLLOWERS:Special Mount|1	DEFINE:SpecialMountLVL|0	BONUS:VAR|SpecialMountLVL|SentinelLVL	COMPANIONLIST:Special Mount|RACETYPE=Animal	SOURCEPAGE:p.443	DESC:Once a day as a standard action, the sentinel summons a Medium or smaller celestial animal (celestial creature template). It carries the same responsibilities as a paladin's special mount and gains the same bonuses with his levels, but remains only 1 hour per level. (Size limit and template are not enforced: choose a Medium or smaller animal and apply the celestial template.)
Dispel Evil	KEY:Sentinel ~ Dispel Evil	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Sentinel Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=SentinelDispel|TIMEUNIT=Week|CASTERLEVEL=SentinelLVL|Dispel Evil	SOURCEPAGE:p.443	DESC:The sentinel can use dispel evil, as the spell, %1 times per week (once at 8th level, one more every four levels; the table misprints 1/week at 12th).|SentinelDispel
Code of Conduct	KEY:Sentinel ~ Code of Conduct	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Sentinel Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.443	DESC:A sentinel must be neutral good and loses all class abilities if he ever willingly commits an evil act. He protects the natural order of the Material Plane from the evil Outer Planes, stays in the wilderness (cities only when necessary, other planes only in dire need) and aids any non-outsider lost or endangered in the wilderness who honors its sanctity. He adventures with non-evil characters and accepts only neutral good henchmen, followers or cohorts.

###Block: Metal Master class features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Metal Master ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Internal	TYPE:Internal	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=WeaponProfMartial|TYPE=ArmorProfHeavy|TYPE=ShieldProfTower	SOURCEPAGE:p.229	DESC:Metal masters are proficient with all simple and martial melee weapons made primarily of metal (here: all simple and martial weapons - choose metal melee weapons), with all armor and with shields (including tower shields).
Spells	KEY:Metal Master ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Metal Master Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.229	DESC:The metal master casts druid spells like a druid (Player's Handbook), with the druid's spell progression; caster level = metal master level. She can lose a prepared spell to cast chill metal, heat metal, rusting grasp, ironwood, transmute metal to wood or repel metal or stone of the same level or lower, and can't cast spells of an alignment opposed to her own or her deity's.
Languages	KEY:Metal Master ~ Languages	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Metal Master Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.229	DESC:Druidic is among her bonus language options (forbidden to teach to nondruids); she knows Terran as a free language.
Mine Sense	KEY:Metal Master ~ Mine Sense	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Metal Master Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SKILL|Knowledge (Dungeoneering),Knowledge (Architecture and Engineering)|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.229	DESC:The metal master gains a +2 bonus on Knowledge (dungeoneering) and Knowledge (architecture and engineering) checks.
Metal Sense	KEY:Metal Master ~ Metal Sense	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Metal Master Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SKILL|Craft (Armorsmithing),Craft (Blacksmithing),Craft (Weaponsmithing)|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.229	DESC:The metal master gains a +2 bonus on Craft (armorsmithing), Craft (blacksmithing) and Craft (weaponsmithing) checks.
Damage Reduction	KEY:Metal Master ~ Damage Reduction	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Metal Master Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:MetalMasterDRB|0	DEFINE:MetalMasterDRCSA|0	DEFINE:MetalMasterDRSA|0	DEFINE:MetalMasterDRA|0	BONUS:VAR|MetalMasterDRB|min(5,floor((MetalMasterLVL-4)/2))*(MetalMasterLVL<16)	BONUS:VAR|MetalMasterDRCSA|5*(MetalMasterLVL>=16)*(MetalMasterLVL<18)	BONUS:VAR|MetalMasterDRSA|5*(MetalMasterLVL>=18)*(MetalMasterLVL<20)	BONUS:VAR|MetalMasterDRA|5*(MetalMasterLVL>=20)	DR:MetalMasterDRB/Bludgeoning|PREVARGT:MetalMasterDRB,0	DR:MetalMasterDRCSA/Cold Iron or Silver or Adamantine|PREVARGT:MetalMasterDRCSA,0	DR:MetalMasterDRSA/Silver or Adamantine|PREVARGT:MetalMasterDRSA,0	DR:MetalMasterDRA/Adamantine|PREVARGT:MetalMasterDRA,0	SOURCEPAGE:p.229	DESC:Damage reduction 1/bludgeoning at 6th level, improving by 1 every two levels to 5/bludgeoning at 14th; at 16th it becomes 5/cold iron, silver or adamantine, at 18th 5/silver or adamantine, and at 20th 5/adamantine.
Major Creation	KEY:Metal Master ~ Major Creation	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Metal Master Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=1|CASTERLEVEL=MetalMasterLVL|Major Creation	SOURCEPAGE:p.229	DESC:Once per day, the metal master can cast major creation (metal objects only) as a caster of her metal master level.
Timeless Body	KEY:Metal Master ~ Timeless Body	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Metal Master Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.229	DESC:The metal master no longer takes ability score penalties for aging and cannot be magically aged (existing penalties remain; bonuses still accrue; she still dies of old age).
Iron Body	KEY:Metal Master ~ Iron Body	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Metal Master Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=1|CASTERLEVEL=MetalMasterLVL|Iron Body	SOURCEPAGE:p.229	DESC:Once per day, the metal master can cast iron body as a caster of her metal master level.

###Block: Sidhe Scholar class features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Sidhe Scholar ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Internal	TYPE:Internal	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=WeaponProfSimple|TYPE=ArmorProfLight|TYPE=ShieldProf	SOURCEPAGE:p.237	DESC:The sidhe scholar is proficient only with simple weapons, light armor and shields (except tower shields), regardless of material.
Spells	KEY:Sidhe Scholar ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Sidhe Scholar Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.237	DESC:The sidhe scholar is a variant druid: she casts druid spells like a druid, with the druid's spell progression, and spontaneously converts prepared spells into summon nature's ally spells; she can't cast spells of an alignment opposed to her own or her deity's. Unless noted, she advances as a druid. A character who takes a level of druid or sidhe scholar can never take levels in the other class.
Intelligentsia	KEY:Sidhe Scholar ~ Intelligentsia	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Sidhe Scholar Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Skill Focus(Knowledge (Nature))	SOURCEPAGE:p.237	DESC:The sidhe scholar gains Skill Focus (Knowledge (nature)) as a bonus feat.
Nature Sense	KEY:Sidhe Scholar ~ Nature Sense	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Sidhe Scholar Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Nature Sense	SOURCEPAGE:p.237	DESC:As the druid: a +2 bonus on Knowledge (nature) and Survival checks.
Wild One	KEY:Sidhe Scholar ~ Wild One	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Sidhe Scholar Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Animal Companion	BONUS:VAR|AnimalCompanionLVL|SidheScholarLVL	SOURCEPAGE:p.237	DESC:The sidhe scholar has a druid's animal companion with sylvan blood: +1 hit point per Hit Die, +2 Dexterity and +2 Charisma (apply by hand). It is always unfriendly toward humanoids other than its master (other druids or rangers can raise it to neutral with wild empathy) and refuses to enter a settlement larger than a thorp, lurking on the outskirts until she returns.
Blessing of the Fey	KEY:Sidhe Scholar ~ Blessing of the Fey	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Sidhe Scholar Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SKILL|Knowledge (Arcana),Survival|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.237	DESC:The fey grant the sidhe scholar a +2 bonus on Knowledge (arcana) and Survival checks.
Sylvan Gifts	KEY:Sidhe Scholar ~ Sylvan Gifts	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Sidhe Scholar Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.237	DESC:The sidhe scholar gains bonus spells as if her Wisdom score were 2 higher than it is (this does not affect her spell DCs). (Not applied automatically: add the extra bonus spells by hand.)
Wild Shape	KEY:Sidhe Scholar ~ Wild Shape	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Sidhe Scholar Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Wild Shape	BONUS:VAR|DruidWildShapeLVL|SidheScholarLVL	SOURCEPAGE:p.237	DESC:As the druid's wild shape, with the druid's progression of uses and forms by her sidhe scholar level (1/day at 5th ... elementals from 16th).
Otherworldly Shifting	KEY:Sidhe Scholar ~ Otherworldly Shifting	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Sidhe Scholar Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.237	DESC:In any wild shape form the sidhe scholar appears alien and strangely beautiful (bright unusual colors, angular features, pointed ears, faintly glowing almond-shaped eyes), slightly smaller and leaner than a typical example, and never the same twice; she rarely blends in with her form's natural kin.
Dark Moon's Secret	KEY:Sidhe Scholar ~ Dark Moon's Secret	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Sidhe Scholar Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SPELLLEVEL:CLASS|Sidhe Scholar=1|Protection from Good|Sidhe Scholar=2|Desecrate|Sidhe Scholar=3|Magic Circle against Good|Sidhe Scholar=4|Unholy Blight|Sidhe Scholar=5|Dispel Good|Sidhe Scholar=6|Create Undead|Sidhe Scholar=7|Blasphemy|Sidhe Scholar=8|Unholy Aura|Sidhe Scholar=9|Summon Monster IX	SOURCEPAGE:p.237	DESC:The sidhe scholar adds the Evil domain spell list to her druid spell list.
Venom Immunity	KEY:Sidhe Scholar ~ Venom Immunity	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Sidhe Scholar Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Venom Immunity	SOURCEPAGE:p.237	DESC:As the druid: immunity to all poisons.
Sylvan Craft	KEY:Sidhe Scholar ~ Sylvan Craft	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Sidhe Scholar Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Craft Staff	SOURCEPAGE:p.237	DESC:The sidhe scholar gains Craft Staff as a bonus feat; her staffs are abstractly beautiful and alien, and she creates them in half the normal time.
A Thousand Faces	KEY:Sidhe Scholar ~ A Thousand Faces	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Sidhe Scholar Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ A Thousand Faces	SOURCEPAGE:p.237	DESC:As the druid: she can change her appearance at will, as the alter self spell (her normal form only).
Timeless Body	KEY:Sidhe Scholar ~ Timeless Body	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Sidhe Scholar Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Timeless Body	SOURCEPAGE:p.237	DESC:As the druid: no ability score penalties for aging, cannot be magically aged.

###Block: Storm Druid class features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Storm Druid ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Internal	TYPE:Internal	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	SOURCEPAGE:p.240	DESC:As the druid (the storm druid advances as a druid unless noted).
Spells	KEY:Storm Druid ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Storm Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:StormDruidThunder|0	SOURCEPAGE:p.240	DESC:The storm druid is a variant druid: she casts druid spells like a druid, with the druid's progression, and can't cast spells of an alignment opposed to her own or her deity's. Instead of summon nature's ally she can lose a prepared spell of equal or higher level to cast obscuring mist (1st), gust of wind (2nd), call lightning (3rd), air walk (4th), call lightning storm (5th), chain lightning (6th), control weather (7th), whirlwind (8th) or storm of vengeance (9th). She keeps nature sense, resist nature's lure, venom immunity, a thousand faces and timeless body and loses all other druid abilities (wild shape, animal companion). A character who takes a level of druid or storm druid can never take levels in the other. Storm druids are almost always chaotic neutral.
Nature Sense	KEY:Storm Druid ~ Nature Sense	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Storm Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Nature Sense	SOURCEPAGE:p.240	DESC:As the druid: a +2 bonus on Knowledge (nature) and Survival checks.
Deafness Immunity	KEY:Storm Druid ~ Deafness Immunity	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Storm Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.240	DESC:The storm druid is immune to deafness, magical or otherwise.
Frightful Presence	KEY:Storm Druid ~ Frightful Presence	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Storm Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.240	DESC:Whenever the storm druid attacks or charges, animals within 30 feet with fewer Hit Dice than she has must make a Will save (DC %1) or be shaken for 4d6 rounds (a successful save makes them immune for 24 hours); from 8th level also magical beasts, fey and vermin, from 16th level creatures of all types. Allies' animal companions and familiars ignore it.|10+floor(StormDruidLVL/2)+CHA
Thunder Strike	KEY:Storm Druid ~ Thunder Strike	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Storm Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.240	DESC:%1/day (at most once per round), declared before a melee attack, the storm druid adds %2d6 electricity damage on a hit and the target must make a Fortitude save (DC %3) or be deafened for 3d6 rounds (permanently from 15th level); a miss still uses it.|StormDruidThunder|(1+(StormDruidLVL>=11)+2*(StormDruidLVL>=20))*1|10+floor(StormDruidLVL/2)+CON
Wind Sense	KEY:Storm Druid ~ Wind Sense	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Storm Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SAVE|Reflex|1+(StormDruidLVL>=9)+(StormDruidLVL>=15)|TYPE=Insight	SOURCEPAGE:p.240	DESC:The storm druid gains a +1 insight bonus on Reflex saving throws (+2 at 9th level, +3 at 15th).
Resist Nature's Lure	KEY:Storm Druid ~ Resist Nature's Lure	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Storm Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Resist Nature's Lure	SOURCEPAGE:p.240	DESC:As the druid: a +4 bonus on saves against the spell-like abilities of fey.
Electricity Resistance	KEY:Storm Druid ~ Electricity Resistance	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Storm Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	BONUS:VAR|ElectricityResistanceBonus|5*floor(StormDruidLVL/5)	SOURCEPAGE:p.240	DESC:The storm druid gains resistance to electricity 5, increasing by 5 every five levels (10 at 10th, 15 at 15th, 20 at 20th).
Venom Immunity	KEY:Storm Druid ~ Venom Immunity	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Storm Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Venom Immunity	SOURCEPAGE:p.240	DESC:As the druid: immunity to all poisons.
Improved Initiative	KEY:Storm Druid ~ Improved Initiative	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Storm Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Improved Initiative	SOURCEPAGE:p.240	DESC:The storm druid gains the Improved Initiative feat.
A Thousand Faces	KEY:Storm Druid ~ A Thousand Faces	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Storm Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ A Thousand Faces	SOURCEPAGE:p.240	DESC:As the druid: she can change her appearance at will, as the alter self spell (her normal form only).
Timeless Body	KEY:Storm Druid ~ Timeless Body	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Storm Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Timeless Body	SOURCEPAGE:p.240	DESC:As the druid (at 14th level for the storm druid): no ability score penalties for aging, cannot be magically aged.

###Block: Totem Druid class features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Totem Druid ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Internal	TYPE:Internal	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	SOURCEPAGE:p.241	DESC:As the druid (the totem druid advances as a druid unless noted).
Spells	KEY:Totem Druid ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Totem Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:TotemDruidShape|0	DEFINE:TotemDruidDire|0	SOURCEPAGE:p.241	DESC:The totem druid is a variant druid: she casts druid spells like a druid, with the druid's progression, spontaneously converts prepared spells into summon nature's ally, and can't cast spells of an alignment opposed to her own or her deity's. Unless noted, she advances as a druid. A character who takes a level of druid or totem druid can never take levels in the other.
Nature Sense	KEY:Totem Druid ~ Nature Sense	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Totem Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Nature Sense	SOURCEPAGE:p.241	DESC:As the druid: a +2 bonus on Knowledge (nature) and Survival checks.
Wild Empathy	KEY:Totem Druid ~ Wild Empathy	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Totem Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Wild Empathy	SOURCEPAGE:p.241	DESC:As the druid.
Totem Animal Companion	KEY:Totem Druid ~ Totem Animal Companion	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Totem Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Animal Companion	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|DMC ~ Animal Companion Alternate	BONUS:VAR|AnimalCompanionLVL|TotemDruidLVL+2	SOURCEPAGE:p.241	DESC:At 1st level the totem druid binds her spirit to an ape, bear, eagle, horse, shark, snake, tiger or wolf. Her animal companion can only be her totem animal (or its dire form); it gains special abilities as if she were two levels higher, and she counts as two levels higher for choosing a dire form (companion level %1).|TotemDruidLVL+2
Totem Shape	KEY:Totem Druid ~ Totem Shape	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Totem Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.241	DESC:As wild shape, but only into her totem animal: %1/day (1/day at 1st level, more at 3rd, 5th, 7th, 11th, 14th, 17th and 20th). From 6th level she can also take the dire form of her totem animal %2/day (in addition to normal uses; 2/day at 12th, 3/day at 18th). From 10th level she can take a celestial (good druid) or fiendish (evil druid) form of her totem animal (a neutral druid chooses the template at 8th level, for good); from 16th level the dire form can have this template too.|TotemDruidShape|TotemDruidDire
Natural Spell	KEY:Totem Druid ~ Natural Spell	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Totem Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Natural Spell	SOURCEPAGE:p.241	DESC:The totem druid gains Natural Spell as a bonus feat.
Woodland Stride	KEY:Totem Druid ~ Woodland Stride	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Totem Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Woodland Stride	SOURCEPAGE:p.241	DESC:As the druid.
Trackless Step	KEY:Totem Druid ~ Trackless Step	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Totem Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Trackless Step	SOURCEPAGE:p.241	DESC:As the druid.
Resist Nature's Lure	KEY:Totem Druid ~ Resist Nature's Lure	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Totem Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Resist Nature's Lure	SOURCEPAGE:p.241	DESC:As the druid: a +4 bonus on saves against the spell-like abilities of fey.
Totem Speech	KEY:Totem Druid ~ Totem Speech	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Totem Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.241	DESC:The totem druid can speak any language she knows while in animal form, and can speak with animals of her totem kind as with speak with animals.
Venom Immunity	KEY:Totem Druid ~ Venom Immunity	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Totem Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Venom Immunity	SOURCEPAGE:p.241	DESC:As the druid: immunity to all poisons.
Timeless Body	KEY:Totem Druid ~ Timeless Body	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Totem Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Timeless Body	SOURCEPAGE:p.241	DESC:As the druid: no ability score penalties for aging, cannot be magically aged.
A Thousand Faces	KEY:Totem Druid ~ A Thousand Faces	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Totem Druid Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ A Thousand Faces	SOURCEPAGE:p.241	DESC:As the druid (at 19th level for the totem druid): she can change her appearance at will, as the alter self spell.
Totem Animal (Ape)	KEY:Totem Druid ~ Totem Animal (Ape)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:TotemDruidTotemAnimal.SpecialQuality	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Ape|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-3	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Ape)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-6	SOURCEPAGE:p.241	DESC:The totem druid is bound to the ape spirit: her animal companion is a ape or its larger or dire form, and her totem shape takes this form.
Totem Animal (Bear)	KEY:Totem Druid ~ Totem Animal (Bear)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:TotemDruidTotemAnimal.SpecialQuality	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Bear (Black)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-3	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Bear (Brown)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-6	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Bear (Polar)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-9	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Bear)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-12	SOURCEPAGE:p.241	DESC:The totem druid is bound to the bear spirit: her animal companion is a bear or its larger or dire form, and her totem shape takes this form.
Totem Animal (Eagle)	KEY:Totem Druid ~ Totem Animal (Eagle)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:TotemDruidTotemAnimal.SpecialQuality	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Eagle	SOURCEPAGE:p.241	DESC:The totem druid is bound to the eagle spirit: her animal companion is a eagle or its larger or dire form, and her totem shape takes this form.
Totem Animal (Horse)	KEY:Totem Druid ~ Totem Animal (Horse)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:TotemDruidTotemAnimal.SpecialQuality	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Horse (Heavy),Companion ~ Horse (Light)	SOURCEPAGE:p.241	DESC:The totem druid is bound to the horse spirit: her animal companion is a horse or its larger or dire form, and her totem shape takes this form.
Totem Animal (Shark)	KEY:Totem Druid ~ Totem Animal (Shark)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:TotemDruidTotemAnimal.SpecialQuality	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Shark (Medium)	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Shark (Large)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-3	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Shark (Huge)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-9	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Shark)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-15	SOURCEPAGE:p.241	DESC:The totem druid is bound to the shark spirit: her animal companion is a shark or its larger or dire form, and her totem shape takes this form.
Totem Animal (Snake)	KEY:Totem Druid ~ Totem Animal (Snake)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:TotemDruidTotemAnimal.SpecialQuality	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Snake (Viper/Medium),Companion ~ Snake (Viper/Small)	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Snake (Constrictor),Companion ~ Snake (Viper/Large)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-3	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Snake (Viper/Huge)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-6	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Snake (Constrictor/Giant)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-9	SOURCEPAGE:p.241	DESC:The totem druid is bound to the snake spirit: her animal companion is a snake or its larger or dire form, and her totem shape takes this form.
Totem Animal (Tiger)	KEY:Totem Druid ~ Totem Animal (Tiger)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:TotemDruidTotemAnimal.SpecialQuality	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Tiger|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-6	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Tiger)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-15	SOURCEPAGE:p.241	DESC:The totem druid is bound to the tiger spirit: her animal companion is a tiger or its larger or dire form, and her totem shape takes this form.
Totem Animal (Wolf)	KEY:Totem Druid ~ Totem Animal (Wolf)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:TotemDruidTotemAnimal.SpecialQuality	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Wolf	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Wolf)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-6	SOURCEPAGE:p.241	DESC:The totem druid is bound to the wolf spirit: her animal companion is a wolf or its larger or dire form, and her totem shape takes this form.
###Block: shared internal abilities
DMC Animal Companion Alternate	KEY:DMC ~ Animal Companion Alternate	CATEGORY:Internal	TYPE:Internal.AnimalCompanionAlternate	SOURCEPAGE:p.550	DESC:Suppresses the PHB druid's standard companion list for classes with their own list (urban druid, shaman, totem druid).

###Block: Wild Reaper class features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Wild Reaper ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Internal	TYPE:Internal	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|Club|Battleaxe|Dagger|Dart|Kama|Nunchaku|Quarterstaff|Scythe|Sickle|Sling|Axe (Throwing)	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=ArmorProfMedium|TYPE=ShieldProf	SOURCEPAGE:p.245	DESC:Wild reapers are proficient with the club, battleaxe, dagger, dart, kama, nunchaku, quarterstaff, scythe, sickle, sling and throwing axe, with all natural attacks, with light and medium armor (padded, leather or hide only - no metal armor, except ironwood) and wooden shields (except tower shields). In metal armor or with a metal shield she can't cast druid spells or use her supernatural or spell-like class abilities while so equipped and for 24 hours after.
Spells	KEY:Wild Reaper ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Wild Reaper Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:WildReaperShape|0	SOURCEPAGE:p.245	DESC:The wild reaper casts druid spells like a druid, with the druid's spell progression, and can't cast spells of an alignment opposed to her own or her deity's; her bonus languages are the druid's.
Animal Companion	KEY:Wild Reaper ~ Animal Companion	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Wild Reaper Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Animal Companion	BONUS:VAR|AnimalCompanionLVL|WildReaperLVL	SOURCEPAGE:p.245	DESC:As the druid's animal companion, except that it must be a carnivorous or omnivorous animal that feeds on carrion (not enforced: choose such an animal).
Nature Sense	KEY:Wild Reaper ~ Nature Sense	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Wild Reaper Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Nature Sense	SOURCEPAGE:p.245	DESC:As the druid: a +2 bonus on Knowledge (nature) and Survival checks.
Woodland Stride	KEY:Wild Reaper ~ Woodland Stride	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Wild Reaper Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Woodland Stride	SOURCEPAGE:p.245	DESC:As the druid.
Spontaneous Casting	KEY:Wild Reaper ~ Spontaneous Casting	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Wild Reaper Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.245	DESC:From 3rd level the wild reaper can lose a prepared spell to cast any summon nature's ally spell of the same level or lower, or soften earth and stone, warp wood, diminish plants, poison, blight, rusting grasp, transmute rock to mud, antilife shell or finger of death of equal or lower level.
Resist Nature's Lure	KEY:Wild Reaper ~ Resist Nature's Lure	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Wild Reaper Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Resist Nature's Lure	SOURCEPAGE:p.245	DESC:As the druid: a +4 bonus on saves against the spell-like abilities of fey.
Wild Shape	KEY:Wild Reaper ~ Wild Shape	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Wild Reaper Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.245	DESC:As polymorph, %1/day (1/day at 5th level; more at 6th, 7th, 10th, 14th and 18th), the wild reaper can take the form of a carnivorous or omnivorous animal that feeds on carrion, Small or Medium (Large from 8th level, Tiny from 11th, Huge from 15th), with Hit Dice no higher than her wild reaper level, for 1 hour per level (%2 hours); standard action, no attack of opportunity; she cannot speak but can communicate with animals of the same general grouping. No elemental forms.|WildReaperShape|WildReaperLVL
Disease Immunity	KEY:Wild Reaper ~ Disease Immunity	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Wild Reaper Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.245	DESC:The wild reaper is immune to all diseases, including supernatural infections like mummy rot and lycanthropy.
Turn Undead	KEY:Wild Reaper ~ Turn Undead	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Wild Reaper Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Basic Turning	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Turn Undead	BONUS:VAR|TurnLevelBase,TurnDamagePlusBase|WildReaperLVL-2	BONUS:VAR|TurnTimesBase|3+CHA|TYPE=Base	BONUS:VAR|TurnCheckBase|CHA|TYPE=Base	SOURCEPAGE:p.245	DESC:The wild reaper turns undead %1 times per day (3 + Charisma modifier) as a cleric two levels lower (%2), without a holy symbol.|3+CHA|WildReaperLVL-2
Resist Death's Lure	KEY:Wild Reaper ~ Resist Death's Lure	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Wild Reaper Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.245	DESC:The wild reaper gains a +4 bonus on saving throws against level drain and death effects (situational - not added to the totals).
Fast Healing	KEY:Wild Reaper ~ Fast Healing	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Wild Reaper Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:FastHealing|0	BONUS:VAR|FastHealing|1+2*(WildReaperLVL>=20)	SOURCEPAGE:p.245	DESC:The wild reaper heals %1 hit points per round (fast healing 1; 3 at 20th level).|1+2*(WildReaperLVL>=20)
Ability Damage Healing	KEY:Wild Reaper ~ Ability Damage Healing	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Wild Reaper Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.245	DESC:The wild reaper heals %1 point(s) of ability damage to all damaged ability scores each round (2 at 20th level), as long as she has at least 1 point of Constitution.|1+(WildReaperLVL>=20)
Timeless Body	KEY:Wild Reaper ~ Timeless Body	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Wild Reaper Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Timeless Body	SOURCEPAGE:p.245	DESC:As the druid: no ability score penalties for aging, cannot be magically aged.

###Block: Wind Walker class features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Wind Walker ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Internal	TYPE:Internal	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|Club|Dagger|Dart|Javelin|Quarterstaff|Scimitar|Shortbow|Sling|Spear	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=ArmorProfLight|TYPE=ShieldProf	SOURCEPAGE:p.247	DESC:Wind walkers are proficient with the club, dagger, dart, javelin, quarterstaff, scimitar, shortbow, composite shortbow, sling and spear, with all natural attacks, with light armor (no metal armor, except ironwood) and wooden shields (except tower shields). In metal armor or with a metal shield he can't cast druid spells or use his supernatural or spell-like class abilities while so equipped and for 24 hours after.
Spells	KEY:Wind Walker ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Wind Walker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:WindWalkerFeather|0	DEFINE:WindWalkerWhisper|0	DEFINE:WindWalkerFly|0	DEFINE:WindWalkerElemental|0	SOURCEPAGE:p.247	DESC:The wind walker casts druid spells like a druid, with the druid's spell progression, and can't cast spells of an alignment opposed to his own or his deity's. He can lose a prepared spell to cast any summon nature's ally spell (the ally must be able to fly) or druid spell with the air descriptor of the same level or lower. Druidic is among his bonus language options; he knows Auran as a free language.
Aerial Companion	KEY:Wind Walker ~ Aerial Companion	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Wind Walker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Animal Companion	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|DMC ~ Animal Companion Alternate	BONUS:VAR|AnimalCompanionLVL|WindWalkerLVL	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Eagle,Companion ~ Hawk,Companion ~ Owl	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Bat),Hippogriff|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-3	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Eagle (Giant),Arrowhawk (Juvenile)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-6	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Griffon,Arrowhawk (Adult)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-9	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Dragonne|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-12	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Arrowhawk (Elder)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-15	SOURCEPAGE:p.247	DESC:The wind walker has a flying animal companion advancing as a druid's: eagle, hawk or owl; alternatives at an adjusted level: dire bat or hippogriff (-3), giant eagle, giant owl or juvenile arrowhawk (-6), griffon or adult arrowhawk (-9), dragonne (-12), elder arrowhawk (-15). (The giant owl exists with Dungeonscape.)
Aerial Empathy	KEY:Wind Walker ~ Aerial Empathy	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Wind Walker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.247	DESC:As wild empathy, but for magical beasts and animals with the air subtype or the ability to fly: 1d20 + %1 (wind walker level + Charisma modifier).|WindWalkerLVL+CHA
Zephyr Spellcasting	KEY:Wind Walker ~ Zephyr Spellcasting	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Wind Walker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	BONUS:CASTERLEVEL|DESCRIPTOR.Air|1	BONUS:DC|DESCRIPTOR.Air|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.247	DESC:The wind walker casts druid spells with the air descriptor at +1 caster level and +1 save DC.
Feather Fall	KEY:Wind Walker ~ Feather Fall	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Wind Walker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=WindWalkerFeather|CASTERLEVEL=WindWalkerLVL|Feather Fall	SOURCEPAGE:p.247	DESC:The wind walker can cast feather fall %1/day (1/day at 2nd level, 2 at 5th, 3 at 8th); caster level = wind walker level.|WindWalkerFeather
Whispering Wind	KEY:Wind Walker ~ Whispering Wind	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Wind Walker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=WindWalkerWhisper|CASTERLEVEL=WindWalkerLVL|Whispering Wind	SOURCEPAGE:p.247	DESC:The wind walker can cast whispering wind %1/day (1/day at 3rd level, 2 at 7th, 3 at 11th); caster level = wind walker level.|WindWalkerWhisper
Air Mastery	KEY:Wind Walker ~ Air Mastery	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Wind Walker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.247	DESC:Airborne creatures take a -1 penalty on attack and damage rolls against the wind walker.
Friend of the Winds	KEY:Wind Walker ~ Friend of the Winds	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Wind Walker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.247	DESC:The wind walker counts as two size categories larger when determining the effects of severe winds on him.
Fly	KEY:Wind Walker ~ Fly	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Wind Walker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=WindWalkerFly|CASTERLEVEL=WindWalkerLVL|Fly	SOURCEPAGE:p.247	DESC:The wind walker can cast fly %1/day (1/day at 7th level, 2 at 10th, 3 at 13th); caster level = wind walker level.|WindWalkerFly
Air Spell Immunity	KEY:Wind Walker ~ Air Spell Immunity	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Wind Walker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.247	DESC:The wind walker is immune to spells with the air descriptor, as though they failed to penetrate spell resistance; he can suppress the immunity for a specific effect (such as wind walk) as a standard action, and reactivate it the same way.
Air Domain	KEY:Wind Walker ~ Air Domain	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Wind Walker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Domain|AUTOMATIC|Air	SOURCEPAGE:p.247	DESC:The wind walker receives the granted power of the Air domain at 12th level; from 14th level he prepares and casts the Air domain spell of each level once per day like a cleric (not usable for spontaneous casting).
Timeless Body	KEY:Wind Walker ~ Timeless Body	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Wind Walker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Timeless Body	SOURCEPAGE:p.247	DESC:As the druid: no ability score penalties for aging, cannot be magically aged.
Elemental Shape	KEY:Wind Walker ~ Elemental Shape	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Wind Walker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.247	DESC:As polymorph, %1/day (1/day at 16th level, 2 at 18th, 3 at 20th), the wind walker can take the form of a Small, Medium or Large air elemental (Huge at 20th), Hit Dice no higher than his wind walker level, for 1 hour per level; he gains its extraordinary, supernatural and spell-like abilities and feats but keeps his creature type.|WindWalkerElemental

###Block: Winter Warden class features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Winter Warden ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Internal	TYPE:Internal	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	SOURCEPAGE:p.249	DESC:The winter warden has the same proficiencies and restrictions as the druid.
Spells	KEY:Winter Warden ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Winter Warden Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:WinterWardenShape|0	SOURCEPAGE:p.249	DESC:The winter warden casts druid spells like a druid, with the druid's spell progression, and can't cast spells of an alignment opposed to his own or his deity's; his bonus languages are the druid's.
Animal Companion	KEY:Winter Warden ~ Animal Companion	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Winter Warden Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Animal Companion	BONUS:VAR|AnimalCompanionLVL|WinterWardenLVL	SOURCEPAGE:p.249	DESC:As the druid's animal companion.
Cold Casting	KEY:Winter Warden ~ Cold Casting	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Winter Warden Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	BONUS:CASTERLEVEL|DESCRIPTOR.Cold|1	BONUS:DC|DESCRIPTOR.Cold|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.249	DESC:The winter warden casts all spells (including spell-like abilities) with the cold descriptor at +1 caster level and +1 save DC.
Nature Sense	KEY:Winter Warden ~ Nature Sense	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Winter Warden Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Nature Sense	SOURCEPAGE:p.249	DESC:As the druid: a +2 bonus on Knowledge (nature) and Survival checks.
Wild Empathy	KEY:Winter Warden ~ Wild Empathy	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Winter Warden Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Wild Empathy	SOURCEPAGE:p.249	DESC:As the druid, but without the usual penalty against magical beasts of the cold subtype.
Ray of Frost	KEY:Winter Warden ~ Ray of Frost	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Winter Warden Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SPELLLEVEL:CLASS|Winter Warden=0|Ray of Frost	SOURCEPAGE:p.249	DESC:Ray of frost is added to the winter warden's spell list as a 0-level spell (prepared and cast as part of his normal druid spells).
Drift Stride	KEY:Winter Warden ~ Drift Stride	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Winter Warden Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.249	DESC:The winter warden can move across the top of snow without stepping into it or being impeded, similar to water walk (magically manipulated snow still affects him).
Trackless Step	KEY:Winter Warden ~ Trackless Step	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Winter Warden Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Trackless Step	SOURCEPAGE:p.249	DESC:As the druid.
Ice Stride	KEY:Winter Warden ~ Ice Stride	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Winter Warden Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.249	DESC:The winter warden moves across ice without stepping onto it or being impeded, similar to water walk: entering an icy square costs no extra movement and Balance, Tumble and Climb DCs there are not increased for him (no protection from the cold; magically manipulated ice still affects him).
Wild Shape	KEY:Winter Warden ~ Wild Shape	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Winter Warden Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.249	DESC:As polymorph, %1/day (1/day at 6th level; more at 7th, 8th, 11th, 14th and 19th), the winter warden can take the form of any Small or Medium animal (Large from 10th level, Huge from 16th), usually an arctic one, with Hit Dice no higher than his winter warden level, for 1 hour per level (%2 hours); standard action, no attack of opportunity; he cannot speak but can communicate with animals of the same general grouping.|WinterWardenShape|WinterWardenLVL
Resistance to Cold	KEY:Winter Warden ~ Resistance to Cold	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Winter Warden Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	BONUS:VAR|ColdResistanceBonus|5+5*(WinterWardenLVL>=12)+10*(WinterWardenLVL>=15)	SOURCEPAGE:p.249	DESC:The winter warden gains resistance to cold %1 (5 at 9th level, 10 at 12th, 20 at 15th).|5+5*(WinterWardenLVL>=12)+10*(WinterWardenLVL>=15)
Wall of Ice	KEY:Winter Warden ~ Wall of Ice	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Winter Warden Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=1|CASTERLEVEL=WinterWardenLVL|Wall of Ice	SOURCEPAGE:p.249	DESC:Once per day, the winter warden can cast wall of ice as a caster of his winter warden level.
Otiluke's Freezing Sphere	KEY:Winter Warden ~ Otiluke's Freezing Sphere	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Winter Warden Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=1|CASTERLEVEL=WinterWardenLVL|Freezing Sphere	SOURCEPAGE:p.249	DESC:Once per day, the winter warden can cast Otiluke's freezing sphere as a caster of his winter warden level.
Immunity to Cold	KEY:Winter Warden ~ Immunity to Cold	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Winter Warden Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Immunity to Cold	SOURCEPAGE:p.249	DESC:The winter warden is immune to cold damage.
Polar Ray	KEY:Winter Warden ~ Polar Ray	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Winter Warden Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=1|CASTERLEVEL=WinterWardenLVL|Polar Ray	SOURCEPAGE:p.249	DESC:Once per day, the winter warden can cast polar ray as a caster of his winter warden level.

###Block: Ancestral Speaker class features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Ancestral Speaker ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Internal	TYPE:Internal	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=WeaponProfSimple|TYPE=ArmorProfMedium|TYPE=ShieldProf	SOURCEPAGE:p.148	DESC:The ancestral speaker is proficient with all simple weapons, with light and medium armor, and with shields (except tower shields).
Spells	KEY:Ancestral Speaker ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Ancestral Speaker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:AncestralSpeakerCommunion|0	SOURCEPAGE:p.148	DESC:The ancestral speaker prays to his ancestors for divine spells, prepared and cast like a cleric's from the cleric spell list with the cleric's progression (without domains; the text does not name the list - the cleric list is assumed). He can't cast spells of an alignment opposed to his own.
Bonus Class Skills	KEY:Ancestral Speaker ~ Bonus Class Skills	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Ancestral Speaker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.148	DESC:The ancestral speaker chooses any two cross-class skills to become class skills (taught by his ancestors).
Ancestral Communion	KEY:Ancestral Speaker ~ Ancestral Communion	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Ancestral Speaker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.148	DESC:%1/day (once at 1st level, one more every five levels), the ancestral speaker asks his ancestors for help with one specific skill: a competence bonus of +%2 (his Charisma modifier + class level) for 1 + Charisma bonus rounds, usable even untrained or for skills he normally can't use. From 9th level he may instead, once per day, ask them questions as the commune spell cast by a cleric of his level.|AncestralSpeakerCommunion|CHA+AncestralSpeakerLVL
Holy Presence	KEY:Ancestral Speaker ~ Holy Presence	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Ancestral Speaker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.148	DESC:The ancestral speaker is his own holy symbol: he casts spells with a divine focus component without one.
Death Talker	KEY:Ancestral Speaker ~ Death Talker	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Ancestral Speaker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.148	DESC:A +%1 bonus on Diplomacy, Bluff, Intimidate and Sense Motive checks against undead (+2 at 4th level, +2 more every four levels).|2*floor(AncestralSpeakerLVL/4)
Improved Resurrection	KEY:Ancestral Speaker ~ Improved Resurrection	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Ancestral Speaker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.148	DESC:Anyone raised or resurrected by the ancestral speaker still loses a level, but drops only to the three-quarter mark of the old level (instead of the halfway point).

###Block: Arcane Disciple class features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Arcane Disciple ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Internal	TYPE:Internal	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=WeaponProfSimple|TYPE=ArmorProfMedium|TYPE=ShieldProf	SOURCEPAGE:p.149	DESC:The arcane disciple is proficient with all simple weapons, with light and medium armor, and with shields (except tower shields).
Spells	KEY:Arcane Disciple ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Arcane Disciple Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.149	DESC:The arcane disciple prepares and casts divine spells like a cleric from the cleric spell list with the cleric's progression; she has no domains. She can't cast spells of an alignment opposed to her own.
Arcane to Divine	KEY:Arcane Disciple ~ Arcane to Divine	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Arcane Disciple Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SPELLLEVEL:CLASS|Arcane Disciple=1|Magic Aura|Arcane Disciple=2|Identify|Arcane Disciple=3|Dispel Magic|Arcane Disciple=4|Imbue with Spell Ability|Arcane Disciple=5|Spell Resistance|Arcane Disciple=6|Antimagic Field|Arcane Disciple=7|Spell Turning|Arcane Disciple=8|Protection from Spells|Arcane Disciple=9|Mage's Disjunction	SOURCEPAGE:p.149	DESC:At every level the arcane disciple chooses one arcane spell from the bard or sorcerer/wizard list, at least one level lower than the highest-level divine spell she can cast, adds it to her cleric spell list and casts it as a divine spell from then on (record the chosen spells by hand). All Magic domain spells are added to her list as divine spells (magic aura 1st ... Mage's disjunction 9th), although she does not have the Magic domain.
Bonus Feats	KEY:Arcane Disciple ~ Bonus Feats	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Arcane Disciple Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.149	DESC:At 1st level, 5th level and every five levels thereafter, the arcane disciple gains a bonus metamagic or item creation feat.

###Block: Aspirant class features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Aspirant ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Internal	TYPE:Internal	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=WeaponProfSimple|TYPE=ArmorProfHeavy|TYPE=ShieldProf	SOURCEPAGE:p.150	DESC:The aspirant is proficient with all simple weapons, with all types of armor, and with shields (except tower shields).
Spells	KEY:Aspirant ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Aspirant Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:AspirantSpontaneous|0	SOURCEPAGE:p.150	DESC:The aspirant prepares and casts divine spells like a cleric from the cleric spell list with the cleric's progression (no domains). She can't cast spells of an alignment opposed to her own.
Spontaneous Casting	KEY:Aspirant ~ Spontaneous Casting	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Aspirant Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.150	DESC:The aspirant can lose any prepared cleric spell to cast any other cleric spell of equal or lower level, %1/day (once at 1st level; 2 at 4th, 3 at 8th, 4 at 12th, 5 at 16th).|AspirantSpontaneous
Shield of the Divine	KEY:Aspirant ~ Shield of the Divine	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Aspirant Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|1+floor(AspirantLVL/5)	SOURCEPAGE:p.150	DESC:The aspirant gains a +%1 bonus to AC (+1 at 1st level, +1 more every five levels), which applies even when she is flat-footed or helpless.|1+floor(AspirantLVL/5)
Divine Counterspell	KEY:Aspirant ~ Divine Counterspell	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Aspirant Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.150	DESC:The aspirant can counter a divine spell without expending a spell, if she can cast spells of its level: ready an action to counterspell as normal, without identifying the spell (a non-divine spell wastes only the action). %1 times per day (3 + Charisma modifier).|3+CHA
Perfect Self	KEY:Aspirant ~ Perfect Self	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Aspirant Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Monk Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Monk ~ Perfect Self	SOURCEPAGE:p.150	DESC:The aspirant becomes a magical creature, with the same effect as the monk ability of the same name.

###Block: Benevolent class features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Benevolent ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Internal	TYPE:Internal	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=WeaponProfSimple|TYPE=ArmorProfHeavy|TYPE=ShieldProfTower	SOURCEPAGE:p.153	DESC:The benevolent is proficient with all simple weapons, with all types of armor, and with shields (including tower shields).
Spells	KEY:Benevolent ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Benevolent Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:BenevolentLuck|0	SOURCEPAGE:p.153	DESC:The benevolent prepares and casts divine spells like a cleric from the cleric spell list with the cleric's progression (no domains). He can't cast spells of an alignment opposed to his own or his deity's.
Spontaneous Casting	KEY:Benevolent ~ Spontaneous Casting	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Benevolent Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.153	DESC:The benevolent can lose any prepared spell of equal or higher level to cast: 0 - cure minor wounds, guidance, resistance; 1st - bless, cure light wounds, sanctuary; 2nd - aid, cure moderate wounds, shield other; 3rd - cure serious wounds, prayer, remove curse; 4th - cure critical wounds, restoration, spell immunity; 5th - atonement, mass cure light wounds; 6th - mass cure moderate wounds, heal; 7th - greater restoration, mass cure serious wounds; 8th - mass cure critical wounds; 9th - mass heal.
Luck of the Gods	KEY:Benevolent ~ Luck of the Gods	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Benevolent Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.153	DESC:%1/day (once at 4th level; 2 at 8th, 3 at 12th, 4 at 16th, 5 at 20th), with a brief benediction the benevolent blesses another creature within one alignment step of his deity: within 24 hours it may reroll one die roll (as the Luck domain's granted power) and add a luck bonus of +%2 (his Charisma bonus) to one roll - both may apply to the same roll. Not on himself; multiple blessings don't stack.|BenevolentLuck|max(0,CHA)

###Block: Crusader (Cleric) class features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Crusader (Cleric) ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Internal	TYPE:Internal	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=WeaponProfSimple|TYPE=ArmorProfHeavy|TYPE=ShieldProfTower	SOURCEPAGE:p.155	DESC:The crusader is proficient with all simple weapons, with all types of armor, and with shields (including tower shields), and with one martial weapon of her choice, as though she had the Martial Weapon Proficiency feat.
Spells	KEY:Crusader (Cleric) ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Crusader (Cleric) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:CrusaderClericFoes|0	DEFINE:CrusaderClericSmite|0	SOURCEPAGE:p.155	DESC:The crusader prepares and casts divine spells like a cleric from the cleric spell list with the cleric's progression (no domains). She can't cast spells of an alignment opposed to her own or her deity's. (Keyed "Crusader (Cleric)" - Tome of Battle's crusader is a different class.)
Deific Foe	KEY:Crusader (Cleric) ~ Deific Foe	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Crusader (Cleric) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.155	DESC:The crusader has %1 deific foe(s) (one at 1st level, another at 6th, 11th and 16th), deities opposed to her own god: a +4 morale bonus on attack and damage rolls against their worshipers.|CrusaderClericFoes
Turn Foe's Followers	KEY:Crusader (Cleric) ~ Turn Foe's Followers	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Crusader (Cleric) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.155	DESC:The crusader can turn or destroy worshipers of her deific foes like a cleric's turn undead (crusader level %1), %2 times per day (3 + Charisma modifier); with 5 or more ranks in Knowledge (religion), +2 on these turning checks.|CrusaderClericLVL|3+CHA
Bonus Feats	KEY:Crusader (Cleric) ~ Bonus Feats	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Crusader (Cleric) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.155	DESC:At 3rd level and every five levels thereafter, the crusader gains a bonus feat from the fighter's bonus feat list (Weapon Specialization and Greater Weapon Specialization excluded) or Combat Casting.
Smite	KEY:Crusader (Cleric) ~ Smite	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Crusader (Cleric) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.155	DESC:%1/day (once at 5th level, one more at 10th, 15th and 20th), the crusader smites a foe that does not worship her deity and shares neither her deity's nor her alignment: her Charisma bonus on the attack roll and +%2 damage (crusader level). Smiting a creature that doesn't qualify has no effect, but uses the smite.|CrusaderClericSmite|CrusaderClericLVL

###Block: Evangelist (Cleric) class features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Evangelist (Cleric) ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Internal	TYPE:Internal	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=WeaponProfSimple|TYPE=ArmorProfMedium|TYPE=ShieldProf	SOURCEPAGE:p.161	DESC:The evangelist is proficient with all simple weapons, with light and medium armor, and with shields (except tower shields).
Spells	KEY:Evangelist (Cleric) ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Evangelist (Cleric) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.161	DESC:The evangelist (keyed "Evangelist (Cleric)" - Complete Divine and the Advanced Player's Manual have different evangelists) casts divine spells from the cleric spell list without preparing them, as a sorcerer casts arcane spells (Wisdom 10 + spell level; DC 10 + spell level + Wis modifier; bonus spells from Wisdom). He can't learn a new spell in place of a domain spell known, and can't cast spells of an alignment opposed to his own or his deity's.
Domains	KEY:Evangelist (Cleric) ~ Domains	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Evangelist (Cleric) Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.161	DESC:The evangelist chooses two domains of his deity at 1st level and one more at 5th, 10th, 15th and 20th. He gains their granted powers, and all their domain spells are added to his spells known at the appropriate levels; he does not gain the cleric's extra domain spell slots. (Chosen in the "Evangelist (Cleric) Domain" category among his deity's domains - the PHB domains; as the compendium's Mystic, not as PCGen domains.)

###Block: Evangelist (Cleric) domains (the PHB domains, chosen among the deity's)
Evangelist Domain (Air)	KEY:Evangelist (Cleric) ~ Domain (Air)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EvangelistClericDomain.SpecialQuality	PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Air	ABILITY:Domain|AUTOMATIC|Air	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=1|Obscuring Mist|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,1	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=2|Wind Wall|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,4	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=3|Gaseous Form|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,6	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=4|Air Walk|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,8	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=5|Control Winds|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,10	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=6|Chain Lightning|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,12	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=7|Control Weather|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,14	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=8|Whirlwind|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,16	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=9|Elemental Swarm (Cast as an air spell only)|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,18	SOURCEPAGE:p.162	DESC:The Air domain (his deity must have it): its granted power, and its domain spells (Obscuring Mist, Wind Wall, Gaseous Form, Air Walk, Control Winds, Chain Lightning, Control Weather, Whirlwind, Elemental Swarm (Cast as an air spell only)) as spells known from the level he can cast them.
Evangelist Domain (Animal)	KEY:Evangelist (Cleric) ~ Domain (Animal)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EvangelistClericDomain.SpecialQuality	PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Animal	ABILITY:Domain|AUTOMATIC|Animal	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=1|Calm Animals|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,1	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=2|Hold Animal|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,4	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=3|Dominate Animal|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,6	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=4|Summon Nature's Ally IV|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,8	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=5|Commune with Nature|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,10	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=6|Antilife Shell|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,12	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=7|Animal Shapes|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,14	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=8|Summon Nature's Ally VIII|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,16	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=9|Shapechange|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,18	SOURCEPAGE:p.162	DESC:The Animal domain (his deity must have it): its granted power, and its domain spells (Calm Animals, Hold Animal, Dominate Animal, Summon Nature's Ally IV, Commune with Nature, Antilife Shell, Animal Shapes, Summon Nature's Ally VIII, Shapechange) as spells known from the level he can cast them.
Evangelist Domain (Chaos)	KEY:Evangelist (Cleric) ~ Domain (Chaos)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EvangelistClericDomain.SpecialQuality	PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Chaos	ABILITY:Domain|AUTOMATIC|Chaos	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=1|Protection from Law|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,1	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=2|Shatter|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,4	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=3|Magic Circle against Law|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,6	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=4|Chaos Hammer|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,8	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=5|Dispel Law|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,10	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=6|Animate Objects|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,12	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=7|Word of Chaos|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,14	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=8|Cloak of Chaos|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,16	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=9|Summon Monster IX|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,18	SOURCEPAGE:p.162	DESC:The Chaos domain (his deity must have it): its granted power, and its domain spells (Protection from Law, Shatter, Magic Circle against Law, Chaos Hammer, Dispel Law, Animate Objects, Word of Chaos, Cloak of Chaos, Summon Monster IX) as spells known from the level he can cast them.
Evangelist Domain (Death)	KEY:Evangelist (Cleric) ~ Domain (Death)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EvangelistClericDomain.SpecialQuality	PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Death	ABILITY:Domain|AUTOMATIC|Death	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=1|Cause Fear|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,1	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=2|Death Knell|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,4	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=3|Animate Dead|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,6	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=4|Death Ward|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,8	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=5|Slay Living|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,10	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=6|Create Undead|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,12	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=7|Destruction|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,14	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=8|Create Greater Undead|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,16	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=9|Wail of the Banshee|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,18	SOURCEPAGE:p.162	DESC:The Death domain (his deity must have it): its granted power, and its domain spells (Cause Fear, Death Knell, Animate Dead, Death Ward, Slay Living, Create Undead, Destruction, Create Greater Undead, Wail of the Banshee) as spells known from the level he can cast them.
Evangelist Domain (Destruction)	KEY:Evangelist (Cleric) ~ Domain (Destruction)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:EvangelistClericDomain.SpecialQuality	PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Destruction	ABILITY:Domain|AUTOMATIC|Destruction	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=1|Inflict Light Wounds|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,1	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=2|Shatter|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,4	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=3|Contagion|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,6	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=4|Inflict Critical Wounds|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,8	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=5|Inflict Light Wounds (Mass)|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,10	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=6|Harm|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,12	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=7|Disintegrate|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,14	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=8|Earthquake|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,16	SPELLKNOWN:CLASS|Evangelist (Cleric)=9|Implosion|PREVARGTEQ:EvangelistClericLVL,18	SOURCEPAGE:p.162	DESC:The Destruction domain (his deity must have it): its granted power, and its domain spells (Inflict Light Wounds, Shatter, Contagion, Inflict Critical Wounds, Inflict Light Wounds (Mass), Harm, Disintegrate, Earthquake, Implosion) as spells known from the level he can cast them.
