###Block: Rage Cleric class features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Rage Cleric ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Internal	TYPE:Internal	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=WeaponProfSimple|TYPE=ArmorProfLight|TYPE=ShieldProf	SOURCEPAGE:p.172	DESC:A rage cleric is proficient with all simple weapons, light armor, and shields (except tower shields).
Spells	KEY:Rage Cleric ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Rage Cleric Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.172	DESC:The rage cleric is a variant cleric: he prepares and casts divine spells like a cleric from the cleric spell list with the cleric's progression, and spontaneously converts prepared spells into cure (good) or inflict (evil) spells like a cleric; he has no domains and cannot turn or rebuke undead. He can't be lawful but must be within one step of his deity's alignment. A character who takes a level of cleric or rage cleric can never take levels in the other.
Rage	KEY:Rage Cleric ~ Rage	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Rage Cleric Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Barbarian Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Barbarian ~ Rage	BONUS:VAR|BarbarianRageTimesLVL,BarbarianRagePowerLVL,RageTimesLVL,RagePowerLVL|RageClericLVL	SOURCEPAGE:p.172	DESC:The rage cleric rages as a barbarian of equal level; rage cleric and barbarian levels stack for the number of rages per day and the rage variant available (greater rage, tireless rage, mighty rage).
Greater Rage	KEY:Rage Cleric ~ Greater Rage	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Rage Cleric Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Barbarian Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Barbarian ~ Greater Rage	SOURCEPAGE:p.172	DESC:As the barbarian.
Indomitable Will	KEY:Rage Cleric ~ Indomitable Will	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Rage Cleric Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Barbarian Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Barbarian ~ Indomitable Will	SOURCEPAGE:p.172	DESC:As the barbarian: a +4 bonus on Will saves to resist enchantment spells while raging.
Tireless Rage	KEY:Rage Cleric ~ Tireless Rage	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Rage Cleric Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Barbarian Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Barbarian ~ Tireless Rage	SOURCEPAGE:p.172	DESC:As the barbarian.
Mighty Rage	KEY:Rage Cleric ~ Mighty Rage	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Rage Cleric Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Barbarian Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Barbarian ~ Mighty Rage	SOURCEPAGE:p.172	DESC:As the barbarian.

###Block: Anagakok class features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Anagakok ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Internal	TYPE:Internal	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|Club|Dagger|Crossbow (Heavy)|Crossbow (Light)|Quarterstaff	SOURCEPAGE:p.658	DESC:As the wizard: club, dagger, heavy and light crossbow, quarterstaff; no armor or shields (arcane spell failure).
Spells	KEY:Anagakok ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Anagakok Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:AnagakokFortune|0	SOURCEPAGE:p.658	DESC:The anagakok is a variant wizard: he prepares arcane spells from his spellbook (bark, carved stone or roots) like a wizard, with the wizard's progression, and read magic from memory. He is a specialist of the anagakok school, unique to his tradition: its spells (create water, know direction ... shambler) are on his spell list and can be prepared in any slot, and he prepares one additional spell of the school per spell level each day (the "+1" included in his spells per day - use it for a school spell); +2 on Spellcraft checks to learn school spells. His prohibited schools are always illusion and necromancy. A character who takes a level of wizard or anagakok can never take levels in the other.
Illiteracy	KEY:Anagakok ~ Illiteracy	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Anagakok Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.658	DESC:Except for arcane spell formulas, the anagakok cannot read or write; he may spend 2 skill points to become literate in all languages he speaks. A level in any other class except barbarian makes him literate.
Spontaneous Casting	KEY:Anagakok ~ Spontaneous Casting	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Anagakok Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.658	DESC:The anagakok can lose any prepared spell of 1st level or higher, other than his specialist bonus spell, to cast endure elements.
Wilderness Lore	KEY:Anagakok ~ Wilderness Lore	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Anagakok Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SKILL|Knowledge (Nature),Survival|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.658	DESC:The anagakok gains a +2 bonus on Knowledge (nature) and Survival checks.
Good Fortune	KEY:Anagakok ~ Good Fortune	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Anagakok Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.658	DESC:The anagakok has %1 good fortune points per day (2 at 1st level, +2 at 5th and every five levels): as an immediate action he adds them to any die roll as a luck bonus equal to the points spent, spread over several rolls or all on one; as a readied action he can grant them to an ally he touches.|AnagakokFortune

###Block: Deathwalker class features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Deathwalker ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Internal	TYPE:Internal	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|Club|Dagger|Crossbow (Heavy)|Crossbow (Light)|Quarterstaff	SOURCEPAGE:p.662	DESC:The deathwalker is proficient with the club, dagger, heavy crossbow, light crossbow and quarterstaff, but not with any armor or shield.
Spells	KEY:Deathwalker ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Deathwalker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.662	DESC:The deathwalker prepares arcane spells from the sorcerer/wizard list and her spellbooks like a wizard, with the wizard's progression, as a necromancer specialist: one additional necromancy spell per spell level each day (the "+1" included in her spells per day - use it for a necromancy spell) and two prohibited schools chosen at 1st level (not divination). She knows all 0-level wizard spells not of a prohibited school, three 1st-level spells plus her Intelligence bonus, and two new spells per level; she may select Spell Mastery.
Master of the Dead	KEY:Deathwalker ~ Master of the Dead	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Deathwalker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.662	DESC:The deathwalker can bind skeletons and zombies to her service as with animate dead: a Charisma check (DC 15 + the undead's Hit Dice) commands one she and her allies have not attacked (attacking it breaks control). She controls at most %1 Hit Dice of mindless undead by any means (5 per deathwalker level, animate dead included). She takes a -2 penalty on Fortitude saves to resist negative levels.|5*DeathwalkerLVL
Undead Familiar	KEY:Deathwalker ~ Undead Familiar	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Deathwalker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Familiar	BONUS:VAR|FamiliarLVL|DeathwalkerLVL	SOURCEPAGE:p.662	DESC:The deathwalker gains a familiar by the wizard's rules, but it immediately becomes undead: type undead, Hit Dice d12 (hit points unchanged), no Constitution score, darkvision 60 ft. and the undead traits; its Hit Dice equal its master's for turning, rebuking or bolstering, and only its master can command it (apply the undead changes by hand).
Aura of the Grave	KEY:Deathwalker ~ Aura of the Grave	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Deathwalker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.662	DESC:The deathwalker no longer needs to sleep, is immune to sleep effects and all diseases, and feels less pain; a DC 25 Knowledge (arcana) check reveals her path.
Shroud of Death	KEY:Deathwalker ~ Shroud of Death	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Deathwalker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.662	DESC:A +4 circumstance bonus on saves against poison, paralysis and mind-affecting effects; a 50% chance that extra damage from a critical hit or sneak attack does not affect her (as fortification); she no longer needs to eat or drink (she still breathes); a -2 penalty on Charisma, Bluff and Diplomacy checks against anything but undead.
Mastery of Undeath	KEY:Deathwalker ~ Mastery of Undeath	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Deathwalker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Basic Turning	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Rebuke Undead	BONUS:VAR|TurnLevelBase,TurnDamagePlusBase|DeathwalkerLVL	BONUS:VAR|TurnTimesBase|1+max(0,CHA)|TYPE=Base	BONUS:VAR|TurnCheckBase|CHA|TYPE=Base	SOURCEPAGE:p.662	DESC:The deathwalker rebukes or commands undead as an evil cleric of her deathwalker level (%1), %2 times per day (1 + her Charisma bonus).|DeathwalkerLVL|1+max(0,CHA)
Mantle of Undeath	KEY:Deathwalker ~ Mantle of Undeath	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Deathwalker Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.662	DESC:The deathwalker becomes an undead creature: she loses her Constitution score and the hit points it gave, her Hit Die becomes d12 (hit points unchanged), her type becomes undead with the undead traits; she keeps her racial traits, and her attack, save and other statistics are not recalculated (apply by hand).
Prohibited School (Abjuration)	KEY:Deathwalker ~ Prohibited School (Abjuration)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DeathwalkerProhibitedSchool.SpecialQuality	BONUS:VAR|DeathwalkerProhibitAbjuration|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.662	DESC:The deathwalker gives up the abjuration school: she can never learn or cast its spells.
Prohibited School (Conjuration)	KEY:Deathwalker ~ Prohibited School (Conjuration)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DeathwalkerProhibitedSchool.SpecialQuality	BONUS:VAR|DeathwalkerProhibitConjuration|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.662	DESC:The deathwalker gives up the conjuration school: she can never learn or cast its spells.
Prohibited School (Enchantment)	KEY:Deathwalker ~ Prohibited School (Enchantment)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DeathwalkerProhibitedSchool.SpecialQuality	BONUS:VAR|DeathwalkerProhibitEnchantment|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.662	DESC:The deathwalker gives up the enchantment school: she can never learn or cast its spells.
Prohibited School (Evocation)	KEY:Deathwalker ~ Prohibited School (Evocation)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DeathwalkerProhibitedSchool.SpecialQuality	BONUS:VAR|DeathwalkerProhibitEvocation|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.662	DESC:The deathwalker gives up the evocation school: she can never learn or cast its spells.
Prohibited School (Illusion)	KEY:Deathwalker ~ Prohibited School (Illusion)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DeathwalkerProhibitedSchool.SpecialQuality	BONUS:VAR|DeathwalkerProhibitIllusion|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.662	DESC:The deathwalker gives up the illusion school: she can never learn or cast its spells.
Prohibited School (Transmutation)	KEY:Deathwalker ~ Prohibited School (Transmutation)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:DeathwalkerProhibitedSchool.SpecialQuality	BONUS:VAR|DeathwalkerProhibitTransmutation|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.662	DESC:The deathwalker gives up the transmutation school: she can never learn or cast its spells.

###Block: Filidh class features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Filidh ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Internal	TYPE:Internal	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|Club|Dagger|Quarterstaff|Shortbow	SOURCEPAGE:p.679	DESC:Filidhs are proficient with the club, dagger, quarterstaff and shortbow, but not with any armor or shield.
Spells	KEY:Filidh ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Filidh Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.679	DESC:The filidh is a variant wizard: she prepares arcane spells from the sorcerer/wizard list and her spellbook like a wizard, with the wizard's progression. She does not have the wizard's Scribe Scroll, bonus feats or familiar. (School specialization is not offered here.) A character who takes a level of wizard or filidh can never take levels in the other.
Filidh Knowledge	KEY:Filidh ~ Filidh Knowledge	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Filidh Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Bardic Knowledge	DEFINE:BardicKnowledgeLVL|0	BONUS:VAR|BardicKnowledgeLVL|FilidhLVL	SOURCEPAGE:p.679	DESC:As the bard's bardic knowledge; levels in other classes granting bardic knowledge stack with her filidh levels.
Greater Divining	KEY:Filidh ~ Greater Divining	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Filidh Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	BONUS:CASTERLEVEL|SCHOOL.Divination|floor(FilidhLVL/5)	SOURCEPAGE:p.679	DESC:The filidh casts divination spells as if her caster level were +%1 higher (+1 at 5th level, +2 at 10th, +3 at 15th, +4 at 20th).|floor(FilidhLVL/5)

###Block: Fleshcrafter class features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Fleshcrafter ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Internal	TYPE:Internal	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|Club|Dagger|Crossbow (Heavy)|Crossbow (Light)|Quarterstaff	SOURCEPAGE:p.679	DESC:The fleshcrafter is proficient with the club, dagger, heavy crossbow, light crossbow and quarterstaff, but not with any armor or shield.
Spells	KEY:Fleshcrafter ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Fleshcrafter Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.679	DESC:The fleshcrafter prepares arcane spells from the sorcerer/wizard list and his spellbooks like a wizard, with the wizard's progression, as a necromancer specialist: one additional necromancy spell per spell level each day (the "+1" included in his spells per day - use it for a necromancy spell) and two prohibited schools chosen at 1st level (not divination). He knows all 0-level wizard spells not of a prohibited school, three 1st-level spells plus his Intelligence bonus, and two new spells per level; he may select Spell Mastery. When an ability requires humanoid bodies, corpses of other sizes count as: Small 1/2, Large 4, Huge 16, Gargantuan 64, Colossal 256 Medium corpses.
Craft Construct	KEY:Fleshcrafter ~ Craft Construct	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Fleshcrafter Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Craft Construct	SOURCEPAGE:p.679	DESC:The fleshcrafter gains Craft Construct as a bonus feat.
Stitched Flesh Familiar	KEY:Fleshcrafter ~ Stitched Flesh Familiar	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Fleshcrafter Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.679	DESC:Instead of summoning a familiar, the fleshcrafter builds a construct familiar (value 300 gp) from the body parts of three Medium humanoids he has killed (DC 18 Craft checks, +100 gp of components for the spark of life); he can't create another until it dies. It has the familiar basics and, by his level: natural armor adjustment +%1, Intelligence %2; empathic link, improved evasion and uncanny likeness (DC 20 Spot notes its likeness to its master) at 1st, alertness and share spells at 3rd, deliver touch spells and speak with master at 5th, sustained spirit at 9th (a replacement keeps its predecessor's memories and personality), spell resistance at 11th, scry on familiar at 13th. (No creature statistics in the text - not a companion here.)|floor((FleshcrafterLVL+1)/2)|5+floor((FleshcrafterLVL+1)/2)
Reaper's Touch	KEY:Fleshcrafter ~ Reaper's Touch	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Fleshcrafter Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.679	DESC:When treating a creature with the Heal skill (DC -5), the fleshcrafter may instead double any hit point or ability damage it takes from existing conditions for 24 hours (a dying creature loses 2 hit points per round and cannot stabilize). An observer's Heal check opposed by his result notices the sabotage; such a check or any healing magic ends it.
Brink of Life and Death	KEY:Fleshcrafter ~ Brink of Life and Death	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Fleshcrafter Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.679	DESC:The fleshcrafter can make a coup de grace as a standard action; concentrating as a full-round action, he extends this to his stitched flesh familiar within range of its empathic link.
Forge Flesh	KEY:Fleshcrafter ~ Forge Flesh	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Fleshcrafter Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.679	DESC:The fleshcrafter crafts animated objects from body parts: per 2 HD, the parts of one Medium creature, a DC 20 Craft check and 200 gp of materials; they obey him without question. He creates and controls animated objects of at most %1 total HD (twice his level).|2*FleshcrafterLVL
Master of Life and Death	KEY:Fleshcrafter ~ Master of Life and Death	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Fleshcrafter Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.679	DESC:When the fleshcrafter affects a living creature (not a construct or undead) with a spell, its save DC increases by +1.
Forge Life	KEY:Fleshcrafter ~ Forge Life	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Fleshcrafter Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.679	DESC:The fleshcrafter can create flesh golems for only 5,000 gp (other prerequisites, time and XP as in the Monster Manual), using body parts of at least twenty Medium humanoids he personally killed; any number of them.
Prohibited School (Abjuration)	KEY:Fleshcrafter ~ Prohibited School (Abjuration)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:FleshcrafterProhibitedSchool.SpecialQuality	BONUS:VAR|FleshcrafterProhibitAbjuration|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.679	DESC:The fleshcrafter gives up the abjuration school: he can never learn or cast its spells.
Prohibited School (Conjuration)	KEY:Fleshcrafter ~ Prohibited School (Conjuration)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:FleshcrafterProhibitedSchool.SpecialQuality	BONUS:VAR|FleshcrafterProhibitConjuration|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.679	DESC:The fleshcrafter gives up the conjuration school: he can never learn or cast its spells.
Prohibited School (Enchantment)	KEY:Fleshcrafter ~ Prohibited School (Enchantment)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:FleshcrafterProhibitedSchool.SpecialQuality	BONUS:VAR|FleshcrafterProhibitEnchantment|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.679	DESC:The fleshcrafter gives up the enchantment school: he can never learn or cast its spells.
Prohibited School (Evocation)	KEY:Fleshcrafter ~ Prohibited School (Evocation)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:FleshcrafterProhibitedSchool.SpecialQuality	BONUS:VAR|FleshcrafterProhibitEvocation|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.679	DESC:The fleshcrafter gives up the evocation school: he can never learn or cast its spells.
Prohibited School (Illusion)	KEY:Fleshcrafter ~ Prohibited School (Illusion)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:FleshcrafterProhibitedSchool.SpecialQuality	BONUS:VAR|FleshcrafterProhibitIllusion|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.679	DESC:The fleshcrafter gives up the illusion school: he can never learn or cast its spells.
Prohibited School (Transmutation)	KEY:Fleshcrafter ~ Prohibited School (Transmutation)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:FleshcrafterProhibitedSchool.SpecialQuality	BONUS:VAR|FleshcrafterProhibitTransmutation|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.679	DESC:The fleshcrafter gives up the transmutation school: he can never learn or cast its spells.

###Block: Soul Reaper class features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Soul Reaper ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Internal	TYPE:Internal	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|Club|Dagger|Crossbow (Heavy)|Crossbow (Light)|Quarterstaff	SOURCEPAGE:p.696	DESC:The soul reaper is proficient with the club, dagger, heavy crossbow, light crossbow and quarterstaff, but not with any armor or shield.
Spells	KEY:Soul Reaper ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Soul Reaper Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:SoulReaperAncestral|0	SOURCEPAGE:p.696	DESC:The soul reaper prepares arcane spells from the sorcerer/wizard list and her spellbooks like a wizard, with the wizard's progression, as a necromancer specialist: one additional necromancy spell per spell level each day (the +1 included in her spells per day - use it for a necromancy spell) and two prohibited schools chosen at 1st level (not divination). She knows all 0-level wizard spells not of a prohibited school, three 1st-level spells plus her Intelligence bonus, and two new spells per level; she may select Spell Mastery.
Inquisitor of the Grave	KEY:Soul Reaper ~ Inquisitor of the Grave	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Soul Reaper Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=1|CASTERLEVEL=SoulReaperLVL|Speak with Dead	SOURCEPAGE:p.696	DESC:Once per day, the soul reaper can use speak with dead as the spell, following all its guidelines and restrictions.
Spiritual Vassal	KEY:Soul Reaper ~ Spiritual Vassal	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Soul Reaper Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	FOLLOWERS:Familiar|1	DEFINE:FamiliarLVL|0	BONUS:VAR|FamiliarLVL|SoulReaperLVL	COMPANIONLIST:Familiar|Companion ~ Spiritual Vassal	SOURCEPAGE:p.696	DESC:Through a vile ritual (100 gp of outsiders' blood and bone and a humanoid slain in sacrifice) the soul reaper binds minor spirits into a spiritual vassal that serves as her familiar (loyal as a familiar; its loss has a familiar's drawbacks); as a free action she can immobilize it with agony. By her level: natural armor +%1, Intelligence %2; alertness, empathic link, improved evasion and share spells at 1st, deliver touch spells at 3rd, speak with master at 5th, spell resistance at 11th, scry on familiar at 13th. (PCGen applies the standard familiar table; the vassal's higher Intelligence by hand.)|floor((SoulReaperLVL+1)/2)|9+floor((SoulReaperLVL+1)/2)
Ancestral Knowledge	KEY:Soul Reaper ~ Ancestral Knowledge	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Soul Reaper Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.696	DESC:%1/day (1 at 5th level, +1 at 9th, 13th, 17th), while her vassal can communicate with her, the soul reaper draws on its memories for one of: memories of past lives (+5 competence on one skill for 1 minute), speech of the ancients (speak and read one language for 1 minute), talents of the elders (use a feat she qualifies for for 1 minute).|SoulReaperAncestral
Bind Spirit	KEY:Soul Reaper ~ Bind Spirit	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Soul Reaper Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.696	DESC:With a readied standard action at the moment a victim reaches -10 hit points or is destroyed, the soul reaper traps its spirit in a gem worth 500 gp or more (Will DC %1 resists) for 1 day per soul reaper level; it can't be restored to life. Once per day while bound: one truthful yes/no answer, or one of its languages for 1 hour, or one of its skills at its ranks for 1 minute (trained); the soul is then released.|15+INT
Bonus Feat	KEY:Soul Reaper ~ Bonus Feat	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Soul Reaper Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.696	DESC:At 10th and 20th level, the soul reaper gains a bonus metamagic, item creation or necromantic feat she qualifies for (Spell Focus and Greater Spell Focus offered; other necromantic feats by hand).
Spawn Undead Servitor	KEY:Soul Reaper ~ Spawn Undead Servitor	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Soul Reaper Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.696	DESC:With a ritual costing 500 gp per Hit Die, the soul reaper forces a bound soul into a skeleton or zombie: it permanently gains the soul's base attack bonus (if higher), skill ranks, weapon and armor proficiencies, feats and Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma, with her alignment; the soul then moves on. It counts as 1.5 times its Hit Dice against turning; its CR is its base CR + 1/4 of the soul's CR.
Prohibited School (Abjuration)	KEY:Soul Reaper ~ Prohibited School (Abjuration)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SoulReaperProhibitedSchool.SpecialQuality	BONUS:VAR|SoulReaperProhibitAbjuration|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.696	DESC:The soul reaper gives up the abjuration school: she can never learn or cast its spells.
Prohibited School (Conjuration)	KEY:Soul Reaper ~ Prohibited School (Conjuration)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SoulReaperProhibitedSchool.SpecialQuality	BONUS:VAR|SoulReaperProhibitConjuration|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.696	DESC:The soul reaper gives up the conjuration school: she can never learn or cast its spells.
Prohibited School (Enchantment)	KEY:Soul Reaper ~ Prohibited School (Enchantment)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SoulReaperProhibitedSchool.SpecialQuality	BONUS:VAR|SoulReaperProhibitEnchantment|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.696	DESC:The soul reaper gives up the enchantment school: she can never learn or cast its spells.
Prohibited School (Evocation)	KEY:Soul Reaper ~ Prohibited School (Evocation)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SoulReaperProhibitedSchool.SpecialQuality	BONUS:VAR|SoulReaperProhibitEvocation|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.696	DESC:The soul reaper gives up the evocation school: she can never learn or cast its spells.
Prohibited School (Illusion)	KEY:Soul Reaper ~ Prohibited School (Illusion)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SoulReaperProhibitedSchool.SpecialQuality	BONUS:VAR|SoulReaperProhibitIllusion|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.696	DESC:The soul reaper gives up the illusion school: she can never learn or cast its spells.
Prohibited School (Transmutation)	KEY:Soul Reaper ~ Prohibited School (Transmutation)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SoulReaperProhibitedSchool.SpecialQuality	BONUS:VAR|SoulReaperProhibitTransmutation|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.696	DESC:The soul reaper gives up the transmutation school: she can never learn or cast its spells.

###Block: Wild Defender class features
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Wild Defender ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Internal	TYPE:Internal	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=WeaponProfMartial|TYPE=ArmorProfLight|TYPE=ShieldProf	SOURCEPAGE:p.498	DESC:As the ranger (the wild defender advances as a ranger unless noted): simple and martial weapons, light armor, shields (except tower shields).
Spells	KEY:Wild Defender ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Wild Defender Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.498	DESC:The wild defender is a variant ranger: he prepares and casts divine spells from the ranger spell list like a ranger (Wisdom), by his own table from 1st level (a 0 means bonus spells only); caster level half his wild defender level. (The compendium's text breaks off before the spellcasting rules - the ranger list and caster level are assumed.) He loses the ranger's favored enemy, bonus feats/combat style, camouflage and hide in plain sight. A character who takes a level of ranger or wild defender can never take levels in the other.
Smite Evil	KEY:Wild Defender ~ Smite Evil	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Wild Defender Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Paladin Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Paladin ~ Smite Evil	BONUS:VAR|PaladinSmiteEvilLVL|WildDefenderLVL	SOURCEPAGE:p.498	DESC:As the paladin: 1/day, +1 at 5th level and every five levels (5/day at 20th); Charisma bonus on the attack roll, +1 damage per level. Wild defender and paladin levels stack for uses per day and extra damage.
Natural Lore	KEY:Wild Defender ~ Natural Lore	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Wild Defender Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SKILL|Knowledge (Nature),Survival|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.498	DESC:The wild defender has a +2 bonus on Knowledge (nature) and Survival checks.
Wild Empathy	KEY:Wild Defender ~ Wild Empathy	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Wild Defender Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Ranger Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Ranger ~ Wild Empathy	SOURCEPAGE:p.498	DESC:As the ranger.
Woodland Stride	KEY:Wild Defender ~ Woodland Stride	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Wild Defender Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Ranger Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Ranger ~ Woodland Stride	SOURCEPAGE:p.498	DESC:As the ranger (at 2nd level for the wild defender).
Trackless Step	KEY:Wild Defender ~ Trackless Step	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Wild Defender Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Trackless Step	SOURCEPAGE:p.498	DESC:The wild defender leaves no trail in natural surroundings and cannot be tracked (he may leave a trail if desired).
Resist Nature's Lure	KEY:Wild Defender ~ Resist Nature's Lure	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Wild Defender Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Resist Nature's Lure	SOURCEPAGE:p.498	DESC:A +4 bonus on saving throws against the spell-like abilities of fey.
Animal Companion	KEY:Wild Defender ~ Animal Companion	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Wild Defender Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Animal Companion	BONUS:VAR|AnimalCompanionLVL|floor(WildDefenderLVL/2)	SOURCEPAGE:p.498	DESC:As the ranger's animal companion (at 5th level for the wild defender; effective druid level half his level).
Rebuke Nature	KEY:Wild Defender ~ Rebuke Nature	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Wild Defender Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.498	DESC:The wild defender rebukes (but does not command) creatures of nature as an evil cleric rebukes undead, %1 times per day (3 + Charisma modifier), as a cleric three levels lower (%2): animals from 6th level, vermin from 8th, plants from 12th, fey from 14th, oozes from 18th, elementals from 20th.|3+CHA|WildDefenderLVL-3
Evasion	KEY:Wild Defender ~ Evasion	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Wild Defender Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Ranger Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Ranger ~ Evasion	SOURCEPAGE:p.498	DESC:As the ranger.

###Block: Horselord class features
Proficiencies	KEY:Horselord ~ Proficiencies	CATEGORY:Internal	TYPE:Internal	ABILITY:Barbarian Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Barbarian ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	SOURCEPAGE:p.103
Battle Ecstasy	KEY:Horselord ~ Battle Ecstasy	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Horselord Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.103	DESC:Instead of raging, the horselord enters battle ecstasy %1 times per day (as often as a barbarian rages): +4 Dexterity, +4 Constitution and damage reduction 1/- (stacking with his class damage reduction), for as long as a barbarian's rage (3 + his new Constitution modifier rounds), with the same fatigue afterwards (none from 17th level). He can use any skill or feat, but skill checks other than Handle Animal and Ride take a -2 penalty. No greater or mighty equivalents. The horselord loses fast movement and trap sense. A character who takes a level of barbarian or horselord can never take levels in the other.|1+floor(HorselordLVL/4)
Horseman	KEY:Horselord ~ Horseman	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Horselord Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.103	DESC:The horselord takes no penalty on Ride checks for riding bareback and gains a +2 bonus when using any saddle (stacking with a military saddle); he chooses a kind of animal he has ridden as a mount and gains a +2 bonus on Handle Animal checks with that kind (most choose their tribe's mounts).
Animal Companion	KEY:Horselord ~ Animal Companion	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Horselord Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Animal Companion	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|DMC ~ Animal Companion Alternate	BONUS:VAR|AnimalCompanionLVL|floor(HorselordLVL/2)	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Horse (Light),Companion ~ Horse (Heavy)	SOURCEPAGE:p.103	DESC:At 4th level the horselord's mount (owned and ridden for at least two months) becomes an animal companion as a ranger's of his level (effective druid level half his level), but it keeps the animal type and is not a magical beast. A lost mount can be replaced after 1d4 months of searching and a DC 15 Handle Animal check.
Improved Mounted Archery	KEY:Horselord ~ Improved Mounted Archery	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Horselord Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.103	DESC:The horselord gains Improved Mounted Archery as a bonus feat (granted with Complete Warrior, the book defining the feat - dmc_abilities_horselord_cw.lst).
Illiteracy	KEY:Horselord ~ Illiteracy	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Horselord Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Barbarian Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Barbarian ~ Illiteracy	SOURCEPAGE:p.103	DESC:As the barbarian.
Uncanny Dodge	KEY:Horselord ~ Uncanny Dodge	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Horselord Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Barbarian Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Barbarian ~ Uncanny Dodge	BONUS:VAR|UncannyDodgeFlankingLevel|HorselordLVL|TYPE=EachClass.REPLACE	SOURCEPAGE:p.103	DESC:As the barbarian.
Improved Uncanny Dodge	KEY:Horselord ~ Improved Uncanny Dodge	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Horselord Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Barbarian Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Barbarian ~ Improved Uncanny Dodge	SOURCEPAGE:p.103	DESC:As the barbarian.
Damage Reduction	KEY:Horselord ~ Damage Reduction	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Horselord Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:HorselordLVLDR|0	BONUS:VAR|HorselordLVLDR|floor((HorselordLVL-4)/3)	DR:HorselordLVLDR/-	SOURCEPAGE:p.103	DESC:As the barbarian: DR 1/- at 7th level, +1 every three levels (5/- at 19th). (Own entry - the barbarian's ability would subtract one for a character without barbarian levels.)
Indomitable Will	KEY:Horselord ~ Indomitable Will	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Horselord Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Barbarian Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Barbarian ~ Indomitable Will	SOURCEPAGE:p.103	DESC:As the barbarian (while in his rage form).
Tireless Rage	KEY:Horselord ~ Tireless Rage	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Horselord Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Barbarian Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Barbarian ~ Tireless Rage	SOURCEPAGE:p.103	DESC:He is no longer fatigued at the end of his rage form.

###Block: Implacable class features
Proficiencies	KEY:Implacable ~ Proficiencies	CATEGORY:Internal	TYPE:Internal	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=WeaponProfMartial|TYPE=ArmorProfHeavy|TYPE=ShieldProf	SOURCEPAGE:p.104
Resilient Rage	KEY:Implacable ~ Resilient Rage	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Implacable Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.104	DESC:The implacable's rage is a resilient rage, %1 times per day (as often as a barbarian rages), otherwise identical to the barbarian's rage (duration, fatigue - none from 17th level): instead of the normal bonuses it grants +%2 Dexterity and Constitution, +2 on Will saves and damage reduction %3/- (stacking with his class damage reduction) - +4 and 1/- at first, +6 and 2/- from 11th level, +8 and 3/- at 20th. The implacable does not get fast movement. A character who takes a level of barbarian or implacable can never take levels in the other.|1+floor(ImplacableLVL/4)|4+2*(ImplacableLVL>=11)+2*(ImplacableLVL>=20)|1+(ImplacableLVL>=11)+(ImplacableLVL>=20)
Weapon and Armor Proficiency	KEY:Implacable ~ Weapon and Armor Proficiency	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Implacable Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.104	DESC:The implacable is proficient with all simple and martial weapons and with all armor and shields (except tower shields).
Illiteracy	KEY:Implacable ~ Illiteracy	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Implacable Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Barbarian Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Barbarian ~ Illiteracy	SOURCEPAGE:p.104	DESC:As the barbarian.
Uncanny Dodge	KEY:Implacable ~ Uncanny Dodge	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Implacable Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Barbarian Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Barbarian ~ Uncanny Dodge	BONUS:VAR|UncannyDodgeFlankingLevel|ImplacableLVL|TYPE=EachClass.REPLACE	SOURCEPAGE:p.104	DESC:As the barbarian.
Trap Sense	KEY:Implacable ~ Trap Sense	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Implacable Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Barbarian Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Barbarian ~ Trap Sense	BONUS:VAR|TrapSenseBonus|ImplacableLVL/3	SOURCEPAGE:p.104	DESC:As the barbarian: +1 on Reflex saves and AC against traps at 3rd level, +1 more every three levels.
Improved Uncanny Dodge	KEY:Implacable ~ Improved Uncanny Dodge	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Implacable Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Barbarian Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Barbarian ~ Improved Uncanny Dodge	SOURCEPAGE:p.104	DESC:As the barbarian.
Damage Reduction	KEY:Implacable ~ Damage Reduction	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Implacable Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:ImplacableLVLDR|0	BONUS:VAR|ImplacableLVLDR|floor((ImplacableLVL-4)/3)	DR:ImplacableLVLDR/-	SOURCEPAGE:p.104	DESC:As the barbarian: DR 1/- at 7th level, +1 every three levels (5/- at 19th). (Own entry - the barbarian's ability would subtract one for a character without barbarian levels.)
Indomitable Will	KEY:Implacable ~ Indomitable Will	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Implacable Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Barbarian Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Barbarian ~ Indomitable Will	SOURCEPAGE:p.104	DESC:As the barbarian (while in his rage form).
Tireless Rage	KEY:Implacable ~ Tireless Rage	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Implacable Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Barbarian Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Barbarian ~ Tireless Rage	SOURCEPAGE:p.104	DESC:He is no longer fatigued at the end of his rage form.

###Block: Harbinger class features
Spells	KEY:Harbinger ~ Spells	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Harbinger Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.123	DESC:The harbinger is a variant bard: he casts arcane spells from the bard list like a bard (Charisma, without preparation), with the bard's spells per day and known, and has the bard's proficiencies (arcane spell failure ignored in light armor). Alignment: any nonlawful and nongood. A character who takes a level of bard or harbinger can never take levels in the other.
Bardic Knowledge	KEY:Harbinger ~ Bardic Knowledge	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Harbinger Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Bardic Knowledge	DEFINE:BardicKnowledgeLVL|0	BONUS:VAR|BardicKnowledgeLVL|HarbingerLVL	SOURCEPAGE:p.123	DESC:As the bard's bardic knowledge (levels in classes granting bardic knowledge stack).
Bardic Music	KEY:Harbinger ~ Bardic Music	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Harbinger Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.123	DESC:The harbinger uses bardic music %1 times per day (once per harbinger level), but his abilities reverse the bard's: they destroy the morale of others. Unless noted they allow a Will save (DC %2).|HarbingerLVL|10+floor(HarbingerLVL/2)+CHA
Instill Fear	KEY:Harbinger ~ Instill Fear	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Harbinger Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.123	DESC:With 3 or more ranks in a Perform skill, the harbinger instills fear in enemies he can see and who see or hear him, for as long as they hear him and 5 rounds after: a -%1 penalty on saves against charm and fear effects and on attack and weapon damage rolls (-1; -2 at 8th, -3 at 14th, -4 at 20th). Mind-affecting fear effect.|1+(HarbingerLVL>=8)+(HarbingerLVL>=14)+(HarbingerLVL>=20)
Encourage Failure	KEY:Harbinger ~ Encourage Failure	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Harbinger Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.123	DESC:From 3rd level with 6 or more ranks in a Perform skill, one enemy within 30 feet who sees and hears him (and whom he sees) takes a -2 penalty on all rolls for 1 round. Mind-affecting.
Dishearten	KEY:Harbinger ~ Dishearten	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Harbinger Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.123	DESC:From 9th level with 12 or more ranks in a Perform skill, %1 enemy(ies) within 30 feet that hear him sing for a full round cower: -4 on saving throws and AC, for as long as they hear him and up to 5 rounds after (one more creature per three levels beyond 15th). Mind-affecting.|1+max(0,floor((HarbingerLVL-15)/3))
Dirge of Binding	KEY:Harbinger ~ Dirge of Binding	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpellLike.Harbinger Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.123	DESC:From 12th level with 15 or more ranks in a Perform skill, the harbinger paralyzes one target for as long as it can hear him (Will DC %1).|10+floor(HarbingerLVL/2)+CHA
Drain Prowess	KEY:Harbinger ~ Drain Prowess	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Harbinger Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.123	DESC:From 18th level with 21 or more ranks in a Perform skill, up to %1 enemies within 30 feet that hear him sing gain two negative levels for as long as they hear him (never permanent; four targets, one more per three levels beyond 18th).|4+max(0,floor((HarbingerLVL-18)/3))

###Block: Sidewinder Monk class features
Sidewinder Monk	KEY:Sidewinder Monk ~ Sidewinder Monk	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Sidewinder Monk Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:SidewinderMonkFangs|0	SOURCEPAGE:p.374	DESC:The sidewinder monk is a variant monk: she advances as a monk (Hit Die, base attack, saves, flurry of blows, unarmed damage, AC bonus, unarmored speed) and keeps the monk's unarmed strike, flurry, evasion, ki strike, wholeness of body, improved evasion, greater flurry, diamond body, diamond soul, timeless body, tongue of the sun and moon and perfect self; she has no still mind, slow fall, purity of body, abundant step, quivering palm or empty body. Her bonus feats are fixed pairs: Persuasive or Stealthy at 1st, Improved Feint or Mobility at 2nd, Improved Disarm or Improved Trip at 6th (prerequisites not needed). A character who takes a level of monk or sidewinder monk can never take levels in the other.
Silver Tongue	KEY:Sidewinder Monk ~ Silver Tongue	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Sidewinder Monk Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SKILL|Bluff|floor(SidewinderMonkLVL/2)|TYPE=Competence	SOURCEPAGE:p.374	DESC:The sidewinder monk masters deception: a +%1 competence bonus on Bluff checks (+1 at 2nd level, +1 more every even level).|floor(SidewinderMonkLVL/2)
Sneak Attack	KEY:Sidewinder Monk ~ Sneak Attack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Sidewinder Monk Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Sneak Attack	DEFINE:SneakAttackDice|0	BONUS:VAR|SneakAttackDice|floor(SidewinderMonkLVL/3)	SOURCEPAGE:p.374	DESC:As the rogue ability: +%1d6 (+1d6 at 3rd level, +1d6 every three levels); stacks with other sneak attack.|floor(SidewinderMonkLVL/3)
Earthbound	KEY:Sidewinder Monk ~ Earthbound	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Sidewinder Monk Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.374	DESC:A +4 competence bonus on opposed Strength checks to resist bull rush or overrun attempts.
Fangs	KEY:Sidewinder Monk ~ Fangs	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Sidewinder Monk Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.374	DESC:%1/day (once at 4th level, one more every four levels) the sidewinder monk grows fangs for 1 + her Constitution bonus rounds (minimum 1): a bite (1d4 piercing; 1d3 for Small) at her highest attack bonus (-2 on it and all other attacks in a flurry). From 15th level, once per day her bite can slay a living creature: Fortitude DC %2 or die (poison).|SidewinderMonkFangs|10+floor(SidewinderMonkLVL/2)+CON
Intimidating Stance	KEY:Sidewinder Monk ~ Intimidating Stance	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Sidewinder Monk Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	BONUS:SKILL|Intimidate|4|TYPE=Competence	SOURCEPAGE:p.374	DESC:A +4 competence bonus on Intimidate checks (+6 while using her fangs).
Persuasive	KEY:Sidewinder Monk ~ Bonus Feat (Persuasive)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SidewinderMonkBonusFeat1st	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Persuasive	SOURCEPAGE:p.374	DESC:Sidewinder Monk bonus feat (prerequisites not needed).
Stealthy	KEY:Sidewinder Monk ~ Bonus Feat (Stealthy)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SidewinderMonkBonusFeat1st	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Stealthy	SOURCEPAGE:p.374	DESC:Sidewinder Monk bonus feat (prerequisites not needed).
Improved Feint	KEY:Sidewinder Monk ~ Bonus Feat (Improved Feint)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SidewinderMonkBonusFeat2nd	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Improved Feint	SOURCEPAGE:p.374	DESC:Sidewinder Monk bonus feat (prerequisites not needed).
Mobility	KEY:Sidewinder Monk ~ Bonus Feat (Mobility)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SidewinderMonkBonusFeat2nd	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Mobility	SOURCEPAGE:p.374	DESC:Sidewinder Monk bonus feat (prerequisites not needed).
Improved Disarm	KEY:Sidewinder Monk ~ Bonus Feat (Improved Disarm)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SidewinderMonkBonusFeat6th	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Improved Disarm	SOURCEPAGE:p.374	DESC:Sidewinder Monk bonus feat (prerequisites not needed).
Improved Trip	KEY:Sidewinder Monk ~ Bonus Feat (Improved Trip)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SidewinderMonkBonusFeat6th	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Improved Trip	SOURCEPAGE:p.374	DESC:Sidewinder Monk bonus feat (prerequisites not needed).

###Block: Wild Monk class features
Wild Monk	KEY:Wild Monk ~ Wild Monk	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class.Wild Monk Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	DEFINE:WildMonkShape|0	DEFINE:WildMonkElemental|0	SOURCEPAGE:p.379	DESC:The wild monk is a variant monk (lawful neutral only): she advances as a monk (Hit Die, base attack, saves, flurry of blows, unarmed damage, AC bonus, unarmored speed) and keeps the monk's unarmed strike, flurry, evasion, ki strike, purity of body, wholeness of body, improved evasion, greater flurry, diamond body, diamond soul, timeless body, tongue of the sun and moon and perfect self; she has no monk bonus feats, still mind, slow fall, abundant step, quivering palm or empty body. She may freely multiclass with the druid; after any other multiclass option she can gain no more wild monk levels. A character who takes a level of monk or wild monk can never take levels in the other.
Resist Nature's Lure	KEY:Wild Monk ~ Resist Nature's Lure	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Wild Monk Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	ABILITY:Druid Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Druid ~ Resist Nature's Lure	SOURCEPAGE:p.379	DESC:A +4 bonus on saving throws against the spell-like abilities of fey.
Wild Shape	KEY:Wild Monk ~ Wild Shape	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Supernatural.Wild Monk Class Feature.Class Feature.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.379	DESC:As the druid ability, %1/day (once at 6th level; more at 8th, 10th, 14th, 18th and 20th): any Small or Medium animal; Large from 12th level, Tiny from 15th, Huge from 16th; from 19th level also a Small, Medium or Large elemental %2/day (2/day at 20th). Independent of a druid's wild shape (an 11th-level druid/9th-level wild monk wild shapes four times per day as a druid and twice per day as a wild monk, each with its own forms).|WildMonkShape|WildMonkElemental
